window.STORIES = [
{id:"we-the-people-affordable-senior-housing", seo:"How to Find Affordable Senior Housing in the 254", cat:"we-the-people", top:1, city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"We the People: How to find affordable senior housing in the 254, even on a fixed income",
 dek:"Rent tied to income, Medicaid help with assisted living and two free agencies that will walk your family through it. Here's how it works.",
 body:[
  "If you're helping a parent find a place to live, or you're on Social Security yourself and rent keeps climbing, the options can feel like a maze. They aren't as hard to sort out as they look. There are three main kinds of help for seniors in Central Texas, and each one works differently.",
  "<strong>1. Apartments where rent is based on your income.</strong> These are HUD-subsidized senior apartments, many built under a federal program called Section 202. They're generally for people 62 and older whose income is under half of the area median. Residents pay about 30% of their adjusted income in rent, and HUD covers the rest. That means a senior living on $1,200 a month would pay about $360 or less, since some medical and other costs are deducted first. In the 254 these include Golden Haven Apartments in Temple, North Crest Court, North Crest Creekside and Brook Oaks Senior Residences in Waco, Exchange Sunshine Home in Copperas Cove, the senior units at the Clifton Housing Authority and Stephenville Crossing.",
  "<strong>2. Tax-credit senior communities with lower rents.</strong> These are privately run apartments built with federal housing tax credits. Rent is a set amount, not a share of your income, but it's kept below market for renters under an income limit. Local examples include Country Lane Seniors and The Grand Reserve Seniors in Temple, Chisholm Trail Senior Village in Belton, Dripping Springs Senior Village in Waco, McGregor Seniors Apartments, Milam Senior Estates in Cameron and Hunters Chase in Rockdale.",
  "<strong>3. Public housing and vouchers.</strong> Local housing authorities run public housing and Section 8 vouchers, which also cap rent at about 30% of income and are open to seniors. In Temple and Belton call the Central Texas Housing Consortium at 254-773-2009. In Killeen call 254-634-5243, and in Waco call 254-752-0324.",
  "<strong>What about assisted living?</strong> This is where many families get surprised. Medicare does not pay for assisted living or long-term nursing home care when the help is mostly with daily tasks like bathing, dressing and eating. Medicaid can. Texas' Medicaid program for seniors, STAR+PLUS, can pay for care in an assisted living facility or at home for people who qualify medically and financially. There is often an interest list, so it pays to apply early.",
  "<strong>Who to call first.</strong> Two free agencies exist for exactly this. In Bell, Coryell, Lampasas, Milam and Hamilton counties, call the Central Texas Aging & Disability Resource Center at 1-855-937-2372. In McLennan, Bosque, Falls and Hill counties, call the Area Agency on Aging of the Heart of Texas at 254-292-1800. They can screen for Medicaid, explain benefits and point you to openings. Anywhere in Texas, dialing 2-1-1 connects you to help with rent and utilities.",
  "<strong>The catch: waiting lists.</strong> Almost every affordable senior property has one, and some lists only open for a few days at a time. Belton's senior public housing list, for example, last took applications for one week in October 2023. Our advice: apply to several places at once, keep copies of every application, and call back every few months to stay active on the list.",
  "<strong>Checking out a care facility.</strong> Before choosing an assisted living facility or nursing home, look it up on the Texas Health and Human Services provider search, which shows inspection results and whether it takes Medicaid. Medicare's Care Compare site gives nursing homes star ratings. And visit in person, more than once if you can.",
  "We've put all of these places, phone numbers and search tools in one spot on our <a href=\"/real-estate/#senior-living\">Real Estate page</a>. Know a senior community we missed? Let us know."],
 sources:[["HUD: Section 202 Supportive Housing for the Elderly","https://archives.hud.gov/progdesc/2eldrl14.cfm"],["National Low Income Housing Coalition: Section 202 guide","https://nlihc.org/sites/default/files/AG-2025/4-113_Section-202-Housing-for-the-Elderly.pdf"],["Medicare.gov: Long-term care","https://www.medicare.gov/coverage/long-term-care"],["Texas HHS: STAR+PLUS Handbook","https://www.hhs.texas.gov/handbooks/starplus-handbook"],["Area Agency on Aging of Central Texas","https://ctcog.org/aging/"],["Area Agency on Aging of the Heart of Texas","https://www.hotcogtx.gov/health-and-human-services/area-agency-on-aging"],["HUD Multifamily Assisted and LIHTC property data","https://resources.hud.gov/"],["Affordable Housing Online: Belton Housing Authority","https://affordablehousingonline.com/housing-authority/Texas/Belton-Housing-Authority/TX213"]]},
{id:"bell-county-grants-bellcad-runoff", seo:"Bell County Takes $16.75M in Road Grants, Trims Runoff Cost", cat:"government", top:1, city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-17",
 title:"Bell County accepts $16.75 million in road grants, trims cost of appraisal board runoff",
 dek:"Commissioners also canvassed the Nov. 3 election, which drew 44% of the county's registered voters.",
 body:[
  "The Bell County Commissioners Court spent Monday morning on money and elections: it accepted more than $16.75 million in federal grants, certified the Nov. 3 results and approved a cheaper plan for an upcoming appraisal district runoff.",
  "<strong>The grants.</strong> The largest is a $15.74 million award, spread over eight years and sponsored by U.S. Rep. John Carter, for road and bridge work along Riverside Trail, Warrior's Path and Highway 81. It requires no local match. A separate $1 million award, sponsored by U.S. Rep. August Pfluger, targets Chaparral Road and could cover engineering, right-of-way and traffic signals. The court also approved about $25,000 in shared safety equipment with Killeen and Temple.",
  "<strong>The election.</strong> Elections Administrator Desi Roberts reported 112,067 ballots cast out of 253,171 registered voters, a 44.27% turnout. Roughly 80,700 people voted early, about 27,200 on Election Day and about 4,200 by mail.",
  "<strong>The runoff.</strong> No candidate won a majority in the Bell County Appraisal District board race, so James Butts and Gwendolyn Everett meet again on Dec. 12. With state approval, the county will run 21 Election Day sites instead of 42, cutting the estimated cost from about $210,700 to about $111,000. BellCAD reimburses the county for the election.",
  "The court meets next on Monday, Dec. 7."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald / Temple Daily Telegram","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/bell-county-canvasses-november-election-accepts-16-75-million-in-grants/article_fab21c7d-5c44-530b-8b28-c8067084627a.html"]]},

{id:"we-the-people-bellcad-runoff", seo:"Bell County Appraisal Board Runoff Dec. 12: What It Does", cat:"we-the-people", top:1, city:"Bell County", date:"2026-11-18",
 title:"We the People: What the Bell County Appraisal District board does, and why it's on your ballot again Dec. 12",
 dek:"The board doesn't set your tax rate, but it oversees the office that decides what your property is worth.",
 body:[
  "If you own a home or business in Bell County, two numbers drive your property tax bill: the value placed on your property, and the tax rates set by your city, county, school district and other local governments. The Bell County Appraisal District, known as BellCAD, handles the first number.",
  "<strong>What BellCAD does.</strong> The appraisal district appraises every taxable property in the county each year and mails out notices of appraised value. It does not set tax rates and does not collect taxes. Those decisions belong to the elected bodies that levy taxes, such as city councils, the commissioners court and school boards.",
  "<strong>What the board does.</strong> A board of directors oversees the district, including its budget and its chief appraiser. It does not decide individual property values; protests over a specific value go to a separate appraisal review board.",
  "<strong>Why there's a runoff.</strong> This fall was the first election the BellCAD board has held. No candidate topped 50%, so James Butts and Gwendolyn Everett face each other on Saturday, Dec. 12. Early voting runs Nov. 30 through Dec. 8.",
  "<strong>Where to vote.</strong> Expect fewer polling places than in November: the county will use 21 Election Day sites and seven early voting sites. Check the Bell County Elections Office for locations before you go.",
  "<strong>How to be heard.</strong> Appraisal notices typically arrive in spring. If you think your value is wrong, the notice explains how and when to file a protest."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald / Temple Daily Telegram","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/bell-county-canvasses-november-election-accepts-16-75-million-in-grants/article_fab21c7d-5c44-530b-8b28-c8067084627a.html"],["Bell County Elections Office","https://www.bellcountytx.com/departments/elections/Notices.php"]]},

{id:"killeen-charter-amendments-pass", cat:"government", top:1, city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-04",
 title:"Killeen voters approve all eight city charter amendments",
 dek:"Changes cover when city elections are held, how council vacancies are filled and how residents can petition and recall.",
 body:[
  "Killeen voters said yes to every proposed change to the city charter in the Nov. 3 special election, according to unofficial results released by the city.",
  "The amendments came out of the 2026 Charter Review Committee. Among the biggest: Proposition A moves regular city elections to November (22,802 for, 8,898 against), and Proposition B ends the requirement that officeholders resign to run for another seat (19,319 to 11,631).",
  "Other measures change how council vacancies are filled, set timelines for initiative and referendum petitions, and rewrite the rules for recalls. The recall proposals passed by the widest margins, with Proposition H, covering recall of district council members, winning 24,907 to 5,881.",
  "The council scheduled a special meeting for Nov. 17 to canvass and certify the results."],
 sources:[["City of Killeen","https://www.killeentexas.gov/m/newsflash/Home/Detail/3139"]]},

{id:"bell-county-justice-center-annex-price", seo:"Bell County Sets $14.05M Price for Justice Center Annex", cat:"growth", city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-17",
 title:"Bell County locks in $14.05 million construction price for Justice Center Annex",
 dek:"The guaranteed maximum price brings the full project budget to about $16 million.",
 body:[
  "Bell County commissioners on Monday approved a guaranteed maximum price of $14.05 million from Cloud Construction for the Justice Center Annex.",
  "With design and other costs included, the county puts the total project budget at roughly $16 million. A guaranteed maximum price caps what the county pays the builder for the agreed scope of work.",
  "The vote came during the same meeting in which the court accepted $16.75 million in road grants and certified the November election."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald / Temple Daily Telegram","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/bell-county-canvasses-november-election-accepts-16-75-million-in-grants/article_fab21c7d-5c44-530b-8b28-c8067084627a.html"]]},

{id:"belton-amity-rose-closure", seo:"Belton Closes Amity Road and Rose Lane Until February", cat:"growth", top:1, city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-12",
 title:"Belton closes E. Amity Road and Rose Lane intersection until February for 7-Eleven street work",
 dek:"The intersection east of I-35 is shut to all traffic through Feb. 1, 2027.",
 body:[
  "The intersection of E. Amity Road and Rose Lane, just east of I-35 in Belton, closed to all traffic on Monday, Nov. 16. The city expects it to stay closed through Feb. 1, 2027.",
  "The work is street improvements tied to a new 7-Eleven development. The city said closing both roads at once lets the contractor finish faster.",
  "<strong>Detours:</strong> Rose Lane traffic is routed south, and East Amity Road traffic is routed north to Fox Road, with drivers sent along county roads. Signs are posted at each closure point.",
  "Questions go to the City of Belton at 254-933-5800."],
 sources:[["City of Belton","https://www.beltontexas.gov/news_detail_T11_R1447.php"]]},

{id:"sh6-twin-bridges-closures", seo:"SH 6 Twin Bridges Over Lake Waco: Rolling Closures Return", cat:"growth", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-16",
 title:"Rolling closures return to SH 6 Twin Bridges over Lake Waco this week",
 dek:"TxDOT crews are moving precast bridge caps for the bridge rebuild.",
 body:[
  "Drivers on State Highway 6 over Lake Waco should plan for delays this week as TxDOT and its contractor haul precast bridge caps for the Twin Bridges reconstruction.",
  "<strong>Tuesday, Nov. 17:</strong> three intermittent rolling closures between 10 a.m. and 1 p.m., then three slow-roll operations between 8 p.m. and midnight while the caps are set.",
  "<strong>Friday, Nov. 20:</strong> another transport window from 10 a.m. to 1 p.m.",
  "Each rolling closure is expected to last about 20 to 30 minutes. Work earlier in November slipped a day because of weather, so check TxDOT updates before you drive."],
 sources:[["FOX 44 via Yahoo News","https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/twin-bridges-rolling-closures-resume-214656733.html"]]},

{id:"temple-industrial-park-2026", seo:"Temple Industrial Park: East Penn, Sesajal and SeAH Update", cat:"business", also:["real-estate"], top:1, city:"Temple", date:"2026-11-18",
 title:"Temple's industrial park keeps adding up: where East Penn, Sesajal and SeAH stand",
 dek:"Three manufacturers have committed $250 million and about 200 jobs to Temple since 2024.",
 body:[
  "Temple's industrial park on the north side of the city has quietly become one of the busiest manufacturing addresses on I-35. Here is a look at the three biggest commitments announced through the Temple Economic Development Corporation.",
  "<strong>East Penn Manufacturing</strong> announced in April a $110 million expansion of its Temple battery plant. The project adds 175,000 square feet to the existing 393,000-square-foot plant and 48 full-time jobs on top of the roughly 350 people already working there. Construction was slated to start in June 2026, with completion expected by fall 2028.",
  "<strong>Sesajal</strong>, a Mexican maker of edible oils, said in March it will invest $30 million in a 50,000-square-foot refinery, bottling and distribution center on 13 acres, creating 54 jobs. The company targeted a mid-2026 groundbreaking and mid-2027 completion.",
  "<strong>SeAH Superalloy Technologies</strong>, part of South Korea's SeAH Group, picked Temple in 2024 for a $110 million specialty-alloy plant that serves the aviation, power and oil and gas industries. It is expected to bring about 100 jobs.",
  "For job seekers and suppliers, the takeaway is simple: the park is hiring in waves, and the next two years are when much of this capacity comes online."],
 sources:[["Temple EDC: East Penn","https://templeedc.com/east-penn-manufacturing-chooses-temple-for-major-expansion/"],["Temple EDC: Sesajal","https://templeedc.com/leading-food-manufacturer-selects-temple-texas-for-new-u-s-operations/"],["Killeen Daily Herald: SeAH","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/temple-set-to-be-home-to-110-million-steel-foundry-that-brings-100-new-jobs/article_0e94fab7-0967-5233-8ece-ff1309042163.html"]]},

{id:"lacy-lakeview-data-center-explainer", seo:"$10 Billion Data Center Near Lacy Lakeview: What to Know", cat:"growth", city:"Lacy Lakeview", date:"2026-11-18",
 title:"What to know about the $10 billion data center proposed north of Lacy Lakeview",
 dek:"The project needs land, water and Waco's cooperation, and neighbors have organized against it.",
 body:[
  "A developer called Infrakey wants to build a roughly $10 billion data center campus on about 520 acres of farmland north of Lacy Lakeview, near Elm Mott. It would be the largest industrial project in McLennan County's history.",
  "<strong>The partnership.</strong> Lacy Lakeview approved a non-binding agreement in December 2025 to annex the site and provide utilities. Because the land sits in Waco's extraterritorial jurisdiction, Infrakey asked Waco in May 2026 to release it so Lacy Lakeview could annex it.",
  "<strong>The water question.</strong> Published estimates put the campus's need at about 2 million gallons a day at full buildout. Lacy Lakeview has pitched reclaimed wastewater, but that plan depends on infrastructure Waco controls.",
  "<strong>The pushback.</strong> Rural neighbors launched a petition with more than 1,500 signatures, raising concerns about water, power and the area's farm character.",
  "254 Texas Insider will keep tracking the project as Waco, Lacy Lakeview and the developer make their next moves."],
 sources:[["The Texas Tribune","https://www.texastribune.org/2026/05/14/waco-data-center-lacy-lakeview-infrakey-texas/"],["Waco Tribune-Herald","https://wacotrib.com/news/local/government-politics/article_187b88c9-05b5-42de-b6c4-2398d57e7a18.html"],["The Waco Bridge","https://wacobridge.org/2026/01/05/six-storylines-2026-waco/"]]},

{id:"bell-county-new-home-prices", cat:"real-estate", city:"Bell County", date:"2026-11-18",
 title:"What a new home costs in Bell County right now, city by city",
 dek:"Temple has the most new-home communities and the lowest average price among the big cities.",
 body:[
  "If you're shopping for new construction in Bell County, where you buy matters. A snapshot of 83 new-home communities listed on NewHomeSource shows a wide spread in average advertised prices:",
  "<ul><li><strong>Temple:</strong> 11 communities, about $273,600</li><li><strong>Copperas Cove:</strong> 6 communities, about $289,200</li><li><strong>Belton:</strong> 3 communities, about $302,100</li><li><strong>Killeen:</strong> 6 communities, about $331,500</li><li><strong>Salado:</strong> 3 communities, about $430,300</li><li><strong>Nolanville:</strong> 2 communities, about $446,400</li></ul>",
  "These are averages of builders' advertised base prices, not closed sales, so the house you actually buy will vary with lot, upgrades and incentives.",
  "Temple's edge comes from volume: it has nearly twice as many active new-home communities as any other city in the county."],
 sources:[["NewHomeSource: Bell County","https://www.newhomesource.com/communities/tx/killeen-area/bell-county"]]},

{id:"killeen-isd-calendar-food-drive", seo:"Killeen ISD Sets 2027-28 Calendar; Food Drive Through Nov. 19", cat:"education", city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-11",
 title:"Killeen ISD sets 2027-28 calendar; Food for Families drive runs through Nov. 19",
 dek:"School will start Aug. 17, 2027, and end May 26, 2028.",
 body:[
  "The Killeen ISD board approved its 2027-2028 academic calendar on Nov. 11. The first day of school will be Aug. 17, 2027, and the last day will be May 26, 2028.",
  "Meanwhile, the district's annual Food for Families drive runs Nov. 12 through Nov. 19. Students, staff and families can donate nonperishable food, which goes to local food pantries.",
  "The district also recognized four seniors named National Merit Commended Students this fall."],
 sources:[["Killeen ISD","https://www.killeenisd.org/news/"]]},

{id:"temple-college-workforce-award", cat:"education", city:"Temple", date:"2026-11-02",
 title:"Temple College wins regional workforce award in its 100th year",
 dek:"The college earned the 2026 Phoenix Award for Excellence in Workforce.",
 body:[
  "Temple College picked up the 2026 Phoenix Award for Excellence in Workforce during its centennial year, the college announced Nov. 2.",
  "The recognition highlights the college's workforce training programs, a growing pipeline for Bell County employers as manufacturing and health care expand.",
  "The college is also teaming up with Texas A&M University–Central Texas on a two-day symphony orchestra concert series this fall."],
 sources:[["Temple College","https://www.templecollege.edu/news/index.html"]]},

{id:"belton-south-oak-cliff-area-round", seo:"Belton vs. South Oak Cliff: Area Round at Waco ISD Stadium", cat:"sports", top:1, city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-16",
 title:"Belton draws powerhouse South Oak Cliff in area round Thursday at Waco ISD Stadium",
 dek:"The Tigers survived Ennis 35-33 to reach the second round of the 5A Division II playoffs.",
 body:[
  "Belton (8-3) gets a big test in the Class 5A Division II area round: Dallas South Oak Cliff (9-2), which rolled past Whitehouse 46-7 in the bi-district round.",
  "<strong>Kickoff:</strong> Thursday, Nov. 19, 7 p.m., Waco ISD Stadium.",
  "Belton advanced with a 35-33 win over Ennis last week. Several other area teams saw their seasons end in the first round, including Harker Heights (31-27 loss to Red Oak), Killeen Ellison (31-21 loss to Midlothian Heritage) and Lake Belton (55-0 loss to North Crowley)."],
 sources:[["KWTX","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"],["Dallas Morning News: bi-district scores","https://www.dallasnews.com/high-school-sports/football/article/texas-high-school-football-scores-week-bi-district-22528533.php"]]},

{id:"area-round-guide-254", cat:"sports", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-17",
 title:"Game Day guide: every 254 team still alive in the area round",
 dek:"Unbeaten La Vega plays in Belton, and four McLennan County teams hit the road.",
 body:[
  "Here is where to find the area's remaining UIL teams this week:",
  "<ul><li><strong>Belton (8-3) vs. South Oak Cliff (9-2)</strong>, 5A-II: Thursday, 7 p.m., Waco ISD Stadium</li><li><strong>La Vega (11-0) vs. Geronimo Navarro (7-3)</strong>, 4A-II: Friday, 7:30 p.m., UMHB's Crusader Stadium, Belton</li><li><strong>Robinson (9-2) vs. Rockport-Fulton (10-1)</strong>, 4A-II: Friday, San Antonio's Gustafson Stadium</li><li><strong>China Spring (4-7) vs. Stafford (9-2)</strong>, 4A-I: Friday, 7 p.m., Buffalo Stadium, Giddings</li><li><strong>Lorena (9-2) vs. Diboll (8-3)</strong>, 3A-I: Friday, 7:30 p.m., Mustang Stadium, Madisonville</li></ul>",
  "Times and sites can change, so check with each school before you head out. The regional round follows Nov. 26-28."],
 sources:[["KWTX","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"],["Yahoo Sports: statewide area schedule","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/texas-high-school-football-playoffs-175444973.html"]]},

{id:"valor-ctcs-title-games", seo:"Valor Prep and Central Texas Christian Play for State Titles", cat:"sports", city:"Waco / Temple", date:"2026-11-16",
 title:"Waco's Valor Prep and Temple's Central Texas Christian play for private-school state titles",
 dek:"Two 254 programs reached TAPPS championship games.",
 body:[
  "Waco Valor Prep (8-3) meets Keller Harvest (5-6) for the TAPPS 6-Man Division II state championship on Friday, Nov. 20, at 7 p.m. at Rocket Field in Robinson. Valor beat San Marcos 62-16 in the playoffs.",
  "Central Texas Christian (9-2) of Temple also reached a TAPPS 11-man state final after a 36-18 semifinal win over Tyler All Saints. Its opponent is unbeaten Dallas First Baptist (12-0); the date and site had not been announced as of Monday."],
 sources:[["KWTX","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"],["Dallas Morning News","https://www.dallasnews.com/high-school-sports/football/article/texas-high-school-football-scores-week-bi-district-22528533.php"]]},

{id:"belton-christmas-chisholm-trail", seo:"Belton Christmas on the Chisholm Trail Adds a Ferris Wheel", cat:"things-to-do", top:1, city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-17",
 title:"Belton's Christmas on the Chisholm Trail adds a 60-foot Ferris wheel this year",
 dek:"Free events Dec. 4-5 downtown, then a themed Christmas Village Dec. 7-11. Parade entries are due Friday.",
 body:[
  "Belton's historic downtown kicks off the season with two free days of Christmas on the Chisholm Trail.",
  "<strong>Friday, Dec. 4:</strong> an outdoor screening of the 2018 film The Grinch at 6 p.m., followed by the Christmas tree lighting at 8 p.m.",
  "<strong>Saturday, Dec. 5:</strong> shopping, food trucks, live music and a kids' zone, with the lighted Christmas parade at 6 p.m. The headliner is a 60-foot Ferris wheel with a six-story view of downtown.",
  "<strong>Want to be in the parade?</strong> Apply by Friday, Nov. 20, at BeltonChamber.com/Parade.",
  "<strong>Belton Christmas Village, Dec. 7-11:</strong> food, crafts and a different theme each night: family games (Dec. 7), Minute to Win It-style games (Dec. 8), comic con night (Dec. 9), Merry Mischief Night (Dec. 10) and Renaissance Night (Dec. 11). Most nights run 5 to 9 p.m.; Renaissance Night runs until 10."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/christmas-on-the-chisholm-trail-belton-puts-on-free-activities/article_ebd04ef0-ac1d-5ef4-9cbe-3b9caa8e6390.html"]]},

{id:"temple-merry-bright-contest", seo:"Temple Merry & Bright Holiday Lights Contest: Enter by Dec. 2", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Temple", date:"2026-11-11",
 title:"Temple's Merry & Bright holiday lights contest is taking entries through Dec. 2",
 dek:"The city's fifth annual contest opened applications Nov. 11.",
 body:[
  "Temple homeowners who go big on holiday lights can enter the city's 5th Annual Merry & Bright Holiday Lights Contest. Applications opened Wednesday, Nov. 11, and close Wednesday, Dec. 2.",
  "For categories, prizes and judging details, contact the City of Temple's public relations office at lspears@templetx.gov."],
 sources:[["City of Temple Newsroom","https://city-of-temple.prowly.com/"]]},

{id:"belton-silver-santa", seo:"Belton Police Silver Santa Gift Drive for Seniors", cat:"sports", city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-13",
 title:"Belton police collecting gifts for seniors in 13th Silver Santa drive",
 dek:"Donations are due Dec. 1 for gift bags delivered to seniors who live alone.",
 body:[
  "The Belton Police Department's 13th annual Silver Santa drive is collecting items for Christmas gift bags for seniors in the city's RU OK program, which checks in on Belton residents 60 and older who live alone without a caretaker.",
  "<strong>What to give:</strong> new socks, blankets, scarves, large-piece jigsaw puzzles, large-print crossword and word-find books, plus small practical items like bandages, calendars, notepads, pens, boxed tissues, magnifying glasses, jar openers and small mirrors.",
  "<strong>Where:</strong> Belton Police Department, the Belton Area Chamber of Commerce or Planet Fitness in Belton, through Dec. 1.",
  "Officers and volunteers will deliver the bags later in December. Seniors can sign up for RU OK at beltontexas.gov/ruok or 254-933-5840."],
 sources:[["City of Belton","https://www.beltontexas.gov/news_detail_T11_R1448.php"]]},

{id:"nasdaq-correction-chip-selloff", seo:"Nasdaq Slides Into Correction as Chip Stocks Sink", cat:"markets", top:1, city:"Wall Street", date:"2026-11-17",
 title:"Nasdaq slides into correction as chip stocks sink ahead of Nvidia earnings",
 dek:"The tech-heavy index is now more than 10% below its Oct. 6 record.",
 body:[
  "A two-day selloff led by semiconductor stocks pushed the Nasdaq Composite into correction territory this week, meaning it closed more than 10% below its record high.",
  "<strong>Monday:</strong> the Nasdaq fell 2.49%, or 626.51 points, to 24,509.76. Its record close was 27,599.89 on Oct. 6.",
  "<strong>Tuesday:</strong> selling spread across Wall Street. The Dow dropped 1.6%, the S&P 500 lost 1% and the Nasdaq slipped another 0.7% to 24,328.38, its lowest level in about seven months. Falling stocks outnumbered rising ones by nearly 3 to 1.",
  "Traders were bracing for Nvidia's quarterly report, which came out after Tuesday's close, along with pressure from new U.S. export controls on AI chips.",
  "<strong>Why it matters here:</strong> most 401(k)s and retirement plans hold big tech stocks through index funds, so a correction shows up in Central Texas account balances even if you don't trade."],
 sources:[["Washington Post / AP","https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2026/11/17/wall-street-stocks-dow-nasdaq/9f975f00-e2cf-11f1-a99e-b3e3805c6b8b_story.html"],["CNBC","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/16/stock-market-today-live-updates.html"],["Mint via TradingView","https://www.tradingview.com/news/moodys:c9b294671702c:0-stock-market-outlook-today-17-nov-sensex-nifty-prediction-djia-s-p-nasdaq-gift-nifty-kospi-nikkei-taiwan-cues/"]]},

{id:"fed-december-rate-hike", seo:"Fed Minutes Point to a December Rate Hike", cat:"markets", top:1, city:"Washington", date:"2026-11-18",
 title:"Fed minutes point to a December rate hike, and some officials want a big one",
 dek:"Hot October inflation has markets expecting the Fed to raise rates at its Dec. 8-9 meeting.",
 body:[
  "The Federal Reserve looks set to raise interest rates again next month, and the debate is now over how much.",
  "<strong>What changed:</strong> consumer prices rose 0.4% in October, more than forecast. Treasury yields jumped after the report, with the 10-year yield back around 5%.",
  "<strong>The minutes:</strong> notes from the Fed's October meeting, released Wednesday, said almost all officials judged further rate increases would likely be appropriate to bring inflation back to 2%.",
  "<strong>How big:</strong> markets have mostly priced in a quarter-point hike at the Dec. 8-9 meeting. Fed Governor Christopher Waller has said a half-point increase should be considered, which would be the Fed's largest hike since 2022.",
  "<strong>What it means for the 254:</strong> higher Fed rates typically push up credit card, auto loan and business line-of-credit rates, and can keep mortgage rates elevated."],
 sources:[["U.S. News & World Report","https://www.usnews.com/news/economy/articles/2026-11-18/fed-poised-to-raise-rates-further-to-stem-inflation"],["The National","https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/economy/2026/11/10/federal-reserve-inflation-interest-rates-december/"],["Forbes","https://www.forbes.com/sites/simonmoore/2026/11/13/waller-floats-prospect-of-larger-december-interest-rate-hike/"]]},

{id:"mortgage-rates-711", cat:"markets", city:"National", date:"2026-11-12",
 title:"Mortgage rates fall for a fourth straight week to 7.11%",
 dek:"Rates are at a seven-week low but still almost a full point higher than a year ago.",
 body:[
  "The average 30-year fixed mortgage rate dropped to 7.11% in Freddie Mac's weekly survey released Nov. 12, down from 7.18% the week before. It was the fourth weekly decline in a row and the lowest level in seven weeks.",
  "The 15-year fixed rate fell to 6.45% from 6.57%.",
  "A year ago, the 30-year rate averaged 6.24% and the 15-year averaged 5.49%, so borrowing is still noticeably more expensive than in 2025.",
  "<strong>For 254 buyers:</strong> with new-home prices in Bell County averaging roughly $274,000 in Temple to $332,000 in Killeen, even small rate moves change monthly payments. Freddie Mac publishes its next survey Thursday."],
 sources:[["Freddie Mac","https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms"]]},

{id:"baylor-football-texas-tech-senior-day", cat:"sports", top:1, city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Baylor hosts ranked Texas Tech on Senior Day after loss at BYU",
 dek:"The Bears (6-4) close their home schedule Saturday at McLane Stadium, then finish at Houston on Nov. 28.",
 body:[
  "Baylor football plays its final home game of 2026 on Saturday, Nov. 21, when the Bears host nationally ranked Texas Tech on Senior Day. Kickoff is set for 2:30 p.m. Central.",
  "<strong>Where Baylor stands:</strong> the Bears are 6-4 overall and 4-3 in the Big 12. They beat Iowa State 42-31 on Nov. 7, then fell 28-7 at No. 10 BYU on Nov. 14.",
  "<strong>What's next:</strong> Baylor closes the regular season at No. 21 Houston on Saturday, Nov. 28. That game kicks off at 8:30 p.m. on ESPN2.",
  "Houston won last year's meeting in Waco 31-24, so the finale doubles as a rivalry rematch."],
 sources:[["Baylor Athletics: Football","https://baylorbears.com/sports/football"],["Baylor Athletics: Houston kickoff time","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/11/16/football-baylor-at-houston-set-for-8-30-pm-on-espn2"],["Wikipedia: Baylor–Houston rivalry","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baylor%E2%80%93Houston_football_rivalry"]]},

{id:"umhb-asc-title-playoff-bye", cat:"sports", top:1, city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-16",
 title:"UMHB wins 20th ASC title, earns first-round playoff bye",
 dek:"The Crusaders (9-1) will host No. 15 Trinity on Nov. 28 in the second round of the Division III playoffs.",
 body:[
  "Mary Hardin-Baylor clinched the American Southwest Conference championship outright on Saturday, Nov. 14, with a 13-3 defensive win over rival Hardin-Simmons at Crusader Stadium in Belton. It is the program's 20th ASC title.",
  "The win moved the Crusaders to 9-1 overall and 5-0 in conference play.",
  "<strong>Playoff path:</strong> No. 13 UMHB received a first-round bye in the 40-team NCAA Division III bracket released Sunday. The Cru will host No. 15 Trinity (9-1) in the second round on Saturday, Nov. 28, at 1 p.m.",
  "The Division III national championship, the Stagg Bowl, is set for Jan. 3 in Salem, Virginia."],
 sources:[["KWTX / UMHB Football","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/15/umhb-shuts-down-hardin-simmons-outright-asc-title/"],["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/kdhpressbox/umhb-embracing-tough-playoff-path/article_eb9ba71f-63ce-4699-b389-6dbe1b691bca.html"],["Southern Athletic Association","https://saa-sports.com/news/2026/11/16/trinity-football-to-play-umhb-in-second-round-of-ncaa-playoffs.aspx"]]},

{id:"baylor-mens-basketball-players-era", seo:"Baylor Men's Basketball Routs Jackson State", cat:"sports", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Baylor men's basketball routs Jackson State, heads to Las Vegas next week",
 dek:"The Bears bounced back from a three-point loss to No. 7 Texas and open the Players Era tournament against Alabama on Nov. 24.",
 body:[
  "Baylor men's basketball beat Jackson State 104-55 at Foster Pavilion on Wednesday, Nov. 18.",
  "The win came three days after a 75-72 loss to No. 7 Texas on Nov. 15, when freshman Kayden Mingo scored 23 points. Baylor also beat Northwestern State, Arkansas-Pine Bluff and Yale to open the season.",
  "<strong>Next up:</strong> the Bears play in the Players Era 16 Championship in Las Vegas, Nov. 24-28, opening against Alabama on Tuesday, Nov. 24.",
  "Coach Scott Drew's team is trying to rebound from a 17-17 season in 2025-26."],
 sources:[["Baylor Athletics","https://baylorbears.com/"],["Baylor Athletics: Men's Basketball","https://baylorbears.com/sports/mens-basketball"],["Baylor Athletics: Players Era","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/5/21/mens-basketball-mbb-to-compete-in-2026-players-era-mens-championship-nov-24-28"]]},

{id:"baylor-womens-basketball-usc", cat:"sports", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Baylor women's basketball faces No. 4 USC Friday night",
 dek:"The Lady Bears have scored 100 or more points twice already this season.",
 body:[
  "Baylor women's basketball takes on No. 4 Southern California on Friday, Nov. 20, at 10 p.m. Central, then returns home to face Northern Kentucky on Sunday, Nov. 22, at 2 p.m.",
  "Coach Nicki Collen's team has opened strong, including a 112-40 win over Texas A&M-Corpus Christi on 254 Day (Nov. 8) and a 100-66 win over East Texas A&M on Nov. 15.",
  "<strong>Also on campus:</strong> Baylor volleyball won a five-set match at Colorado on Nov. 15."],
 sources:[["Baylor Athletics","https://baylorbears.com/"],["Baylor Athletics: Women's Basketball schedule","https://baylorbears.com/sports/womens-basketball/schedule"]]},

{id:"tarleton-state-no1-fcs", seo:"Tarleton State 11-0, No. 1 in FCS Heading Into Playoffs", cat:"sports", city:"Stephenville", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Tarleton State is 11-0 and ranked No. 1 in the FCS heading into the playoffs",
 dek:"The Texans won the United Athletic Conference title in Stephenville, at the west edge of the 254.",
 body:[
  "Tarleton State football is unbeaten at 11-0 (6-0 in the United Athletic Conference) and ranked No. 1 in both the STATS FCS poll and the FCS Coaches poll, as of Nov. 15.",
  "The Texans won the UAC championship and are headed to the FCS playoffs under head coach Todd Whitten, now in his 17th season.",
  "Stephenville sits in the 254 area code, making the Texans one of the area's top college football stories this fall."],
 sources:[["Wikipedia: 2026 Tarleton State Texans football","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Tarleton_State_Texans_football_team"]]},

{id:"temple-college-leopards-basketball", seo:"Temple College Leopards Basketball: Week in Review", cat:"sports", city:"Temple", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Temple College Leopards basketball: men split home week, women win in overtime",
 dek:"Both TC teams are on the road this week as nonconference play wraps up before conference play.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Men:</strong> the Temple College Leopards outlasted Dallas College-Mountain View 103-88 after a 75-68 home loss to nationally ranked Angelina, which pulled away late. The Leopards then traveled to Hobbs, New Mexico, for two Region V games.",
  "<strong>Women:</strong> the Lady Leopards rallied to force overtime and won on a game-winner against Blinn. They played at the TJC Classic in Tyler against Tyler Junior College (Nov. 13) and Butler Community College (Nov. 14), and open the WTC Classic in Snyder against Western Texas College on Nov. 19.",
  "The women opened the season at home on Kirby Johnson Court on Oct. 31 against Palo Alto College, with a sophomore-heavy roster led by returning guards Korina Garcia and Raniyah Hunt.",
  "Home games stream on the Temple College PlaySight channel."],
 sources:[["Temple College Athletics","https://tcleopards.com/"],["Temple College: Women's basketball season opener","https://www.tcleopards.com/sports/wbkb/2026-27/releases/20261030dw37d8"]]},

{id:"college-theatre-254-season", seo:"College Theatre in the 254: Baylor and Temple College Shows", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"College theatre in the 254: what's next at Baylor and Temple College",
 dek:"Baylor Theatre just closed Big Love. Next up: a Shakespeare comedy in February and Mean Girls the musical in the spring.",
 body:[
  "Baylor Theatre wrapped its fall run of <em>Big Love</em>, Charles Mee's comic retelling of an ancient Greek play, on Nov. 15 in Waco. Earlier this fall the department staged <em>Sense & Sensibility</em> and <em>Earth and Sky</em>.",
  "<strong>Coming up at Baylor:</strong> <em>The Complete Works of William Shakespeare (Abridged)</em> runs Feb. 23-28, 2027, and the <em>Mean Girls</em> musical runs April 21 to May 2, 2027.",
  "<strong>Temple College:</strong> TC Theatre gave a free fall musical theatre showcase in October in the Jackson-Graeter Backstage Theatre, inside the Mary Alice Marshall Performing Arts Center. It previewed scenes from upcoming shows.",
  "Baylor's School of Music also holds student recitals and ensemble concerts during the semester. Check the Baylor events calendar for dates."],
 sources:[["Baylor Theatre","https://theatre.artsandsciences.baylor.edu/"],["Central Texas Live Theatre: Baylor productions","https://ctxlivetheatre.com/local_theatres/baylor-university-theatre/productions/"],["Baylor events calendar","https://calendar.web.baylor.edu/?category=All"],["Temple College: Musical Theatre Showcase","https://www.templecollege.edu/events/2026/10/musical-theatre-showcase.html"]]},

{id:"waco-business-roundup-nov-2026", seo:"Waco Business Roundup: 7 Brew, The Chateau and More", cat:"business", top:1, city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Waco business roundup: 7 Brew, Capitol Bearing, The Chateau and a $169M riverfront build",
 dek:"A busy November of ribbon cuttings across Waco, plus what the Barron's Branch construction means for drivers.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Openings:</strong> the Greater Waco Chamber held ribbon cuttings this month for 7 Brew Coffee's newest Waco location at New Road and Franklin Avenue (Nov. 2), an expansion of Anytime Fitness Waco (Nov. 4), Capitol Bearing & Hydraulics (Nov. 6), Pivotal Pathway Massage Therapy & Wellness Center (Nov. 13) and The Chateau Waco (Nov. 17).",
  "<strong>Woodway:</strong> Swim Waco, which started as lessons in a backyard pool, celebrated the grand opening of its new swim facility in Woodway.",
  "<strong>Riverfront:</strong> construction is underway on the $169 million Barron's Branch project along the Brazos. Related road closures, including on University Parks Drive, are affecting drivers and local race routes.",
  "<strong>Restaurants:</strong> Waco Restaurant Week ran Nov. 6-14. Restaurants kept all of their sales, and registration fees went to Keep Waco Beautiful.",
  "Have a Waco opening, expansion or closing to share? <a href=\"/contact/\">Send us a tip.</a>"],
 sources:[["Greater Waco Chamber: Member calendar","https://business.wacochamber.com/membercalendar"],["Greater Waco Chamber: Calendar","https://business.wacochamber.com/events"],["KWTX","https://www.kwtx.com/"],["Westland: Waco this fall","https://westlandrg.com/blog/fall-in-waco-whats-opened-whats-coming-and-where-to-actually-go-this-season"]]},

{id:"killeen-cove-heights-business-roundup-nov-2026", seo:"Killeen, Harker Heights, Copperas Cove Business Roundup", cat:"business", city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-19",
 title:"Killeen, Harker Heights and Copperas Cove business roundup: The Pickle, HOTWORX and big-box buzz",
 dek:"New spots to play, work out and get a haircut in Killeen, while Copperas Cove waits on two possible big-box stores.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Killeen:</strong> The Pickle has soft-opened at 2830 E. Veterans Memorial Blvd. It's a sports bar with pickleball, brick-oven pizza, cornhole and shuffleboard, aimed at families and military members. Owner Ray Constancio says a grand opening is still to come.",
  "HOTWORX gets a ribbon cutting from the Greater Killeen Chamber at 10 a.m. Friday, Nov. 20. Roses & Razors Barber Co., owned by Tyson Skinner, held its grand opening Nov. 3 and is taking appointments.",
  "<strong>Harker Heights:</strong> a 40,000-square-foot Crunch Fitness has been under construction near I-14, part of a wave of new fitness, dining and retail projects between Killeen and Harker Heights.",
  "<strong>Copperas Cove:</strong> two big-box stores may be headed to the Shops at Five Hills on Robert Griffin III Boulevard. Local reports point to Hobby Lobby and Academy Sports, but the city EDC hasn't confirmed the names. Sober Sips, a non-alcoholic bar run by two veterans, is also preparing to open in Cove.",
  "Know about a Bell County opening or closing? <a href=\"/contact/\">Send us a tip.</a>"],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: The Pickle","https://kdhnews.com/business/the-pickle-brings-pickleball-pizza-and-family-entertainment-to-killeen/article_662a9230-e864-49e6-8869-e711ce8e2c03.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Business Briefs","https://kdhnews.com/business/business-briefs/article_3de40525-deaa-4212-86d2-e9ee6ee01928.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Roses & Razors","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/new-barbershop-opens-in-killeen-area/article_9d72e6b9-6025-4d0b-9fb7-70bbfd79ac2f.html"],["KXXV: Development boom","https://www.kxxv.com/news/local-news/in-your-neighborhood/development-boom-brings-new-businesses-to-killeen-and-harker-heights"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Five Hills","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/cove-eyeing-new-big-box-stores-in-five-hills-shopping-center/article_74b153a2-e2e4-4e17-bfa6-4f4127eb0e98.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Sober Sips","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/geared-towards-veterans-a-new-non-alcoholic-bar-will-soon-open-in-copperas-cove/article_00953b5d-dca3-43a4-9a8b-7fc7591e5cac.html"]]},

{id:"copperas-cove-academy-hobby-lobby-confirmed", seo:"Academy and Hobby Lobby Confirmed for Copperas Cove", cat:"business", also:["real-estate"], top:1, city:"Copperas Cove", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"It's official: Academy Sports and Hobby Lobby are coming to Copperas Cove in a $21.3 million build",
 dek:"The city confirmed both stores for a 12-acre site on Robert Griffin III Boulevard, with openings targeted for fall 2027.",
 body:[
  "The big-box rumors in Copperas Cove are now confirmed. City development services director Bobby Lewis told the Killeen Daily Herald that a new Hobby Lobby and an Academy Sports + Outdoors will be built at 276 Robert Griffin III Boulevard, near RGIII Boulevard and MLK Drive, just south of the Shops at Five Hills.",
  "<strong>The money:</strong> a filing by Broadstone Net Lease puts the investment at about $12.96 million for Academy and about $8.33 million for Hobby Lobby, roughly $21.3 million combined. Both stores are listed on 15-year leases, with work starting this month and a target of November 2027 for the projects to be fully up and running.",
  "<strong>The developer:</strong> Collett Properties of Charlotte, N.C., signed a development agreement with the Copperas Cove Economic Development Corp. for the 12.065-acre tract. The EDC is putting in a $350,000 grant, paid in two installments, to reimburse stormwater drainage work. Runoff from about 55 acres of undeveloped land has to cross the site, which had held it back.",
  "<strong>The buildings:</strong> state filings describe a single-story Academy store of about 55,870 square feet, with construction scheduled from March to August 2027. Plans for the roughly 15.9-acre subdivision show two retail buildings of about 55,000 square feet each, around 450 parking spaces, a detention pond and a 2.29-acre outparcel for a future tenant. Collett is advertising fall 2027 openings.",
  "<strong>Why it matters:</strong> Cove shoppers now drive to Killeen or Harker Heights for both chains. The new stores add sales tax revenue on the city's west side and could pull more retail to the open outparcel."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/business/academy-sports-hobby-lobby-coming-to-copperas-cove-as-21-3m-retail-development-moves-forward/article_37f92cac-78eb-46bd-96b3-992119fae124.html"]]},

{id:"killeen-isd-optimization-ellison-town-hall", seo:"Killeen ISD Weighs Closing Ellison High: Town Hall Recap", cat:"education", top:1, city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"485 people pack Ellison High as Killeen ISD weighs closing the 48-year-old campus",
 dek:"The district's final Optimization 2.0 town hall drew its biggest crowd yet. Trustees review feedback Dec. 8 and expect to finalize a plan Dec. 15.",
 body:[
  "More than 485 people filled the Ellison High School auditorium this week for Killeen ISD's third and final town hall on its Optimization 2.0 plan, a two-hour meeting about possible school closures, relocations and rezoning. Earlier sessions drew about 80 people at Shoemaker High and about 165 at Killeen High.",
  "<strong>Why the district is doing this:</strong> enrollment has fallen by more than 5,000 students since the 2022-23 school year, and the district projects losing about $31 million in federal Impact Aid over five years. KISD is weighing 11 different scenarios.",
  "<strong>What could happen to Ellison:</strong> one option, labeled scenario 6c, would close Ellison at the end of the 2027-28 school year and rezone its students to Chaparral, Killeen and Shoemaker high schools. The district estimates that would save $22.6 million in operating costs over five years and avoid $8.1 million in heating, air conditioning and roof work. Ellison opened in 1978.",
  "Another option would move the Early College High School from Fort Hood into Ellison as a school-within-a-school.",
  "<strong>What's next:</strong> no decision has been made. Trustees will review community feedback at a Dec. 8 workshop, and the district expects to finalize the plan at the Dec. 15 board meeting. Any change requires a board vote.",
  "<strong>Also in KISD news:</strong> 17 Killeen ISD seniors earned Academic All-State honors from the Texas High School Coaches Association, and Ellison soprano Alaina Corder was chosen to sing with an international honor choir at Carnegie Hall on Feb. 7."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/news/education/killeen-isd-hosts-final-town-hall-on-proposed-optimization-2-0-plan/article_6024e563-5d12-4a85-8fd6-0097d4feee7e.html"],["KWTX: Good News Friday","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/20/good-news-friday-11202026/"]]},

{id:"ctc-army-additive-manufacturing-contract", seo:"Central Texas College Wins Army 3D Manufacturing Contract", cat:"education", city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Central Texas College wins Army contract to teach Fort Hood soldiers 3D manufacturing",
 dek:"A six-week, five-course program will train III Armored Corps soldiers with no prior experience in design and additive manufacturing.",
 body:[
  "Central Texas College has landed an Army contract to provide additive manufacturing instruction, better known as industrial 3D printing, to soldiers supporting III Armored Corps at Fort Hood. The work ties into the Army Transformation Initiative.",
  "<strong>What soldiers will learn:</strong> the program runs five courses over six weeks, covering engineering design, computer-aided design, reverse engineering, materials science and the Defense Department's qualification standards for additive manufacturing, ending with a capstone project. It is built for soldiers with no prior experience.",
  "<strong>Who's involved:</strong> CTC Chancellor Michele J. Carter, Sam Jackson of the college's engineering and drafting program, and the Phantom X Nexus Advanced Manufacturing Lab at Fort Hood.",
  "<strong>Why it matters:</strong> the ability to print replacement parts in the field can cut repair times, and the skills carry over to civilian manufacturing jobs, a growing sector along the I-14 corridor. The contract's dollar value and start date were not reported."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/news/education/ctc-lands-army-contract-training-soldiers-on-manufacturing-technology/article_f7dadb6c-98bf-48d2-8ca6-0d1054d103b9.html"]]},

{id:"texas-gas-prices-thanksgiving-2026", seo:"Texas Gas Prices for Thanksgiving 2026: Priciest Since 2021", cat:"markets", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Gas is falling, but Texas is still headed for its priciest Thanksgiving at the pump since 2021",
 dek:"The Texas average is $3.20 a gallon, about 50 cents more than last Thanksgiving. Nearly 73 million Americans are expected to drive for the holiday.",
 body:[
  "Prices are dropping ahead of Thanksgiving travel, but not enough to erase the jump from last year. AAA Texas put the statewide average for regular unleaded at $3.20 a gallon on Thursday, Nov. 19. AAA Texas says that could make this the most expensive Thanksgiving for Texas drivers since 2021.",
  "<strong>Compared with past years:</strong> Texans paid an average of $2.70 a gallon last Thanksgiving, $2.65 in 2024 and $2.74 in 2023.",
  "<strong>Nationally:</strong> the U.S. average fell 18 cents in a week to about $3.72, down from $4.30 a month ago but still more than 60 cents above a year ago. AAA says the national average could drop another 15 cents by Thanksgiving Day and avoid topping the record of $3.58 set in 2022. West Texas Intermediate crude settled at $83.26 a barrel on Wednesday.",
  "<strong>Texas is still cheap by comparison:</strong> only North Carolina and Indiana had lower averages. California and Hawaii are above $5.50.",
  "<strong>For 254 travelers:</strong> AAA projects nearly 73 million people will take road trips over the holiday."],
 sources:[["KAUZ NewsChannel 6 / AAA Texas","https://www.newschannel6now.com/2026/11/19/aaa-texas-reports-gas-prices-continue-falling-thanksgiving-approaches/"],["AAA: Gas prices keep dropping","https://gasprices.aaa.com/gas-prices-keep-dropping-as-thanksgiving-approaches/"]]},

{id:"waco-school-leaders-legislature-wish-list", seo:"What Waco, Midway and Connally ISD Want From the Legislature", cat:"government", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"What Waco, Midway and Connally ISD want from the Legislature in January",
 dek:"Local school leaders are asking for more state money, funding based on enrollment and more control over local decisions.",
 body:[
  "With the Texas Legislature set to meet in January, three McLennan County districts are laying out their asks, according to The Waco Bridge.",
  "<strong>Waco ISD:</strong> Chief of Staff Elizabeth Cox said the district wants funding based on enrollment instead of average daily attendance, and wants the per-student basic allotment tied to inflation. She pointed to rising energy, diesel and health care costs.",
  "<strong>Connally ISD:</strong> state-appointed Superintendent Josie Gutierrez said academic gains require more state funding and noted that the state takeover did not come with new money. An after-school enrichment hour added this fall cost $300,000, part of a $1.7 million shortfall in the district's $26.9 million budget.",
  "<strong>Midway ISD:</strong> Superintendent Chris Allen presented draft priorities to the school board Tuesday, including local control over instructional materials and programs, fewer limits on financial decisions and more state money for mandates such as the 2023 armed-officer requirement.",
  "<strong>The backdrop:</strong> the basic allotment went unchanged for six years before lawmakers raised it by $55 in 2025, to $6,215 per student. House Democrats have filed a bill to raise it to $7,500 and index it to inflation. Gov.-elect Gina Hinojosa has said she wants to unwind state takeovers of school districts. Any change to the accountability law would also need to pass the Republican-led Senate."],
 sources:[["The Waco Bridge","https://wacobridge.org/2026/11/19/texas-legislature-public-schools-waco-connally-midway/"]]},

{id:"bell-county-councils-roundup-nov-20", seo:"Bell County Councils: Killeen, Copperas Cove, Nolanville", cat:"government", city:"Bell County", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Bell County council roundup: Killeen holds off on water fees, Cove rejects MUD petition, Nolanville gets a new mayor",
 dek:"A busy week at city halls from Killeen to Copperas Cove, plus a Killeen council seat that will soon need filling.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Killeen:</strong> the City Council tabled proposed water impact fees this week after members raised concerns about the details and about input from stakeholders. Impact fees are one-time charges on new development that help pay for water lines and plants.",
  "<strong>Killeen council seat:</strong> Mayor Pro Tem Jessica Gonzalez, who won a Bell County justice of the peace seat this month, turned in her resignation from the District 1 council seat. She plans to stay on until a replacement is chosen.",
  "<strong>Killeen communication:</strong> council members agreed to take up a protocol next month for how city staff notify the council about significant city business. Gonzalez said she wants timely, consistent notice from the city manager's office, city secretary and assistant city manager.",
  "<strong>Copperas Cove:</strong> the council rejected a petition tied to the proposed Church Mountain municipal utility district and called a runoff election. A candidate later withdrew from the Place 7 runoff, settling that seat.",
  "<strong>Harker Heights:</strong> the council turned down a rezoning request that would have allowed manufactured homes.",
  "<strong>Nolanville:</strong> the city honored longtime Mayor Andy Williams and welcomed new Mayor James Bilberry."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: Water impact fees","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/killeen-council-tables-water-impact-fees-after-concerns-over-details-and-stakeholder-input/article_475a0a0f-53e0-4dd1-bec9-b9abe89d684e.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Gonzalez resignation","https://kdhnews.com/government/gonzalez-turns-in-resignation-intends-to-stay-on-killeen-council-until-replacement-selected/article_0263ac4c-1ad0-4cf3-af25-ef6c69f315eb.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Council protocol","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/killeen-council-agrees-to-bring-up-protocol-for-communication-to-council-next-month/article_dcb61d61-7762-4a22-956a-a2c1996119cf.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Cove MUD petition","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/copperas-cove-council-rejects-church-mountain-mud-petition-calls-runoff-election/article_7320dc46-881e-400e-960a-3890321afc6f.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Cove Place 7","https://kdhnews.com/copperas_cove_herald/cove-council-place-7-seat-set-after-candidate-withdraws/article_b44b22a4-e9cc-4375-abeb-f9a29dccbe6e.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Heights rezoning","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/heights-council-turns-down-rezoning-request-that-would-have-allowed-manufactured-homes/article_8741dbeb-46d4-443b-88c1-7cb88c9dfeec.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Nolanville mayor","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/nolanville-honors-longtime-mayor-andy-williams-welcomes-new-mayor-james-bilberry/article_428c07ee-fd93-4860-8aa0-dc53022a672f.html"]]},

{id:"baylor-athletics-200-million-fueling-greatness", seo:"Baylor Launches $200M Fueling Greatness Athletics Campaign", cat:"sports", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Baylor launches $200 million 'Fueling Greatness' push for athletics",
 dek:"Athletic director Doug McNamee laid out a four-year fundraising initiative covering coaches, scholarships, facilities and faith programs.",
 body:[
  "Baylor Athletics is starting a four-year, $200 million initiative called Fueling Greatness, athletic director Doug McNamee announced in a letter to supporters on Thursday, according to The Baylor Lariat.",
  "<strong>Where the money would go:</strong> four priorities. Resourcing championships (coaching staffs, equipment and travel), scholarships, capital projects such as new facilities and game-day upgrades, and faith and formation programs including chaplaincy and leadership development.",
  "McNamee wrote that supporters \"must lean in together to fund our ambitions for all our teams.\"",
  "<strong>The context:</strong> the Lariat noted that Baylor's estimated football roster spending of $20 million to $23 million trails in-state rivals including Texas, Texas Tech and TCU in the revenue-sharing era. University President Linda Livingstone recently disclosed a projected $30 million operating deficit for fiscal 2027.",
  "<strong>On the field this weekend:</strong> Baylor (6-4) hosts ranked Texas Tech on Senior Day Saturday at McLane Stadium."],
 sources:[["The Baylor Lariat","https://baylorlariat.com/2026/11/20/mcnamee-announces-4-year-200-million-athletics-initiative-in-recent-letter/"],["Fox Sports: Texas Tech at Baylor","https://www.foxsports.com/college-football/texas-tech-red-raiders-vs-baylor-bears-nov-21-2026-game-boxscore-44300"]]},

{id:"area-round-thursday-results-friday-slate", seo:"Belton's Season Ends vs. South Oak Cliff; Bremond Rolls", cat:"sports", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Belton's season ends against South Oak Cliff; Bremond rolls 71-21 as area round continues tonight",
 dek:"Thursday's results and every 254 team playing Friday night.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Belton:</strong> the Tigers' season ended Thursday night at Waco ISD Stadium with a 57-14 loss to Dallas South Oak Cliff in the Class 5A Division II area round. South Oak Cliff returned two punts for touchdowns, covering 77 and 64 yards. Belton finishes 8-4.",
  "<strong>Bremond:</strong> the unbeaten Tigers routed Three Rivers 71-21 in the 2A Division II area round to move to 12-0.",
  "<strong>Axtell:</strong> the Longhorns' perfect season ended with a 28-16 loss to De Leon in the 2A Division I area round in Dublin.",
  "<strong>Tonight's 254 games (Friday, Nov. 20):</strong> La Vega (11-0) vs. Geronimo Navarro at UMHB's Crusader Stadium in Belton; Robinson vs. Rockport-Fulton in San Antonio; Lorena vs. Diboll in Madisonville; China Spring vs. Stafford in Giddings; Cameron Yoe vs. Orangefield in Houston; Rosebud-Lott vs. Flatonia in Manor; Crawford vs. Wellington in Graham; Goldthwaite (11-0) vs. Haskell in San Angelo; San Saba vs. Muenster in Granbury; Aquilla (11-0) vs. Medina in Priddy; Oglesby vs. Union Hill in Oakwood; and Mount Calm vs. Runge in Bartlett. Most kick off at 7 or 7:30 p.m.",
  "<strong>State title on the line:</strong> Waco's Valor Prep plays Keller Harvest for the TAPPS 6-man Division II championship tonight at 7 at Rocket Field in Robinson."],
 sources:[["Dallas Morning News via Yahoo Sports","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/photos-south-oak-cliff-rolls-084438695.html"],["High School Football America: area-round scores","https://highschoolfootballamerica.com/final-scores-from-2nd-round-of-uil-texas-high-school-football-playoff-games-played-november-19-21-2026/"],["KWTX: Area round pairings","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"]]},

{id:"bell-county-weekend-nov-20-22", seo:"Bell County Weekend: Eli Young Band, Holiday Market, Chili", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Bell County", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Weekend in Bell County: Eli Young Band, a holiday market, a chili cook-off and Polar Express pajama night",
 dek:"Plans for Friday through Sunday in Temple, Belton, Killeen and Harker Heights before Thanksgiving week.",
 body:[
  "<strong>Friday, Nov. 20:</strong> Pajama Night with a Polar Express screening at the Mayborn Science Theater at Central Texas College, 7 p.m., $8 per person. Free music bingo at Papa's Cafe in Harker Heights, 7 to 9 p.m. Borderline plays Bo's Barn Dancehall in Temple, 8 p.m., $10 cover.",
  "<strong>Saturday, Nov. 21:</strong> the Eli Young Band plays Temple's Cultural Arts Center at 7:30 p.m. Belton Market Days brings a holiday market with vendors, food trucks and live music to 121 N. East St., 9 a.m. to 4 p.m. Belton's Wake and Brew hosts its second annual chili cook-off starting at 9 a.m. with pony rides and a bounce house. Bold Republic Brewing in Temple holds its family-friendly Mustache Bash, 1 to 5 p.m. Armor of God Outreach hosts a 5K Run and Walk for the Unhoused at Lions Club Park in Killeen starting at 8 a.m.",
  "<strong>Sunday, Nov. 22:</strong> the seventh annual Giving Thanks and Share Your Blessings event at Killeen's E Center, 3 to 7 p.m. Martian Folk plays Fire Street Pizza in Belton at noon.",
  "<strong>Saturday markets:</strong> Belton Farmers Market (7 a.m. to noon), Harker Heights Farmers Market (9 a.m. to 1 p.m., running through Dec. 12) and the Lampasas Farmers Market on the courthouse square (9 a.m. to 2 p.m.).",
  "Times and prices can change, so check with organizers before you go. Hosting an event? <a href=\"/contact/\">Send it to us.</a>"],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: Out and About","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/out-and-about-multiple-events-upcoming-in-the-central-texas-area/article_d2b0c076-9522-4922-9e2d-8512a177e9ae.html"]]},

{id:"mortgage-rates-jump-728-254-payment", seo:"Mortgage Rates Hit 7.28%: What It Means for a 254 Payment", cat:"real-estate", top:1, city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"Mortgage rates jump back to 7.28%. Here's what that does to a payment on a typical 254 home",
 dek:"Freddie Mac's weekly average snapped a four-week slide. Daily rates are closer to 7.45%, more than a full point above a year ago.",
 body:[
  "Mortgage rates are climbing again. Freddie Mac's weekly survey put the average 30-year fixed rate at 7.28% on Thursday, Nov. 19, up from 7.11% a week earlier and 6.26% a year ago. The 15-year average rose to 6.66% from 6.45%.",
  "Mortgage News Daily, which tracks rates every weekday, had the average top-tier 30-year rate at 7.45% on Nov. 19, after briefly topping 7.5% earlier in the week.",
  "<strong>What it means for a 254 buyer:</strong> the median listing price in the Killeen-Temple metro was $275,000 in October, according to Realtor.com. With 10% down, principal and interest at 7.28% comes to about $1,693 a month. At last year's 6.26%, the same loan would have been about $1,526, a difference of roughly $167 a month, or about $2,000 a year. Property taxes and insurance are on top of that.",
  "<strong>The upside for buyers:</strong> prices have softened. Killeen-Temple list prices were down about 7% from a year earlier and Waco's were down about 4%, and homes are taking 77 to 79 days to sell. That gives buyers more room to negotiate on price, repairs or a rate buydown paid by the seller.",
  "<strong>Try your own numbers</strong> with the payment calculator on our <a href=\"/real-estate/#housing-dashboard\">254 Housing Dashboard</a>, which tracks rates and local market data and is updated daily."],
 sources:[["Freddie Mac PMMS","https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms"],["Mortgage News Daily: Daily rate index","https://www.mortgagenewsdaily.com/mortgage-rates/mnd"],["Realtor.com via FRED: Killeen-Temple median list price","https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MEDLISPRI28660"]]},

{id:"254-housing-market-october-2026", seo:"254 Housing Report: Prices Slipping, Homes Sitting Longer", cat:"real-estate", top:1, city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-20",
 title:"254 housing report: Prices are slipping and homes are sitting longer. What it means for buyers, sellers and owners",
 dek:"October numbers for Killeen-Temple, Waco and the Austin metro next door, plus the national picture.",
 body:[
  "Central Texas housing cooled further in October as mortgage rates stayed above 7%. Here's where the 254 stands, using Realtor.com listing data for local metros, Unlock MLS and the Austin Board of REALTORS for the Austin metro, and the National Association of REALTORS for the nation.",
  "<strong>Killeen-Temple metro:</strong> the median listing price was $275,000, down from $297,000 a year earlier. Active listings slipped to 2,448 from 2,524, and the median home spent 77 days on the market, compared with 80 a year ago.",
  "<strong>Waco metro:</strong> the median listing price was about $303,500, down from $315,000 a year earlier. Active listings rose slightly to 1,659, and the median home spent 79 days on the market, down from 100 a year ago.",
  "<strong>Austin metro, next door:</strong> closed sales fell 11.4% from a year earlier to 2,114, and the median sold price dropped 6.9% to about $404,800, according to Unlock MLS. Williamson County's median fell 9.2% to $375,250. Months of inventory rose to 6.2. Falling Austin prices can pull some buyers who might have moved north to the 254 back toward Austin.",
  "<strong>Nationally:</strong> existing-home sales fell 5.5% in October to an annual pace of 3.75 million, the slowest since August 2010, NAR reported. The national median price was $416,700, up just 0.4% from a year earlier, with 5.1 months of supply.",
  "<strong>If you're buying:</strong> you have time and leverage. Ask for repairs, closing-cost help or a seller-paid rate buydown, and compare at least three lenders.",
  "<strong>If you're selling:</strong> price it right on day one. Overpriced homes are the ones sitting past 90 days and taking cuts.",
  "<strong>If you own:</strong> values have flattened, not crashed. Watch for your 2027 appraisal notice in the spring and compare it with recent nearby sales before deciding whether to protest.",
  "Track rates and these numbers on our <a href=\"/real-estate/#housing-dashboard\">254 Housing Dashboard</a>. This is general information, not financial advice."],
 sources:[["Realtor.com via FRED: Killeen-Temple","https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MEDLISPRI28660"],["Realtor.com via FRED: Waco","https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MEDLISPRI47380"],["Unlock MLS: October 2026 Central Texas Housing Report","https://www.unlockmls.com/news/october-2026-central-texas-housing-report"],["NAR: October existing-home sales","https://www.nar.realtor/newsroom/existing-home-sales-decreased-5-5-percent-october-nar-report"]]},
{id:"area-round-friday-la-vega-lorena-yoe-regionals", seo:"La Vega, Robinson, Lorena, Cameron Yoe Win Area Round", cat:"sports", top:1, city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"summary",
 title:"La Vega, Robinson, Lorena and Cameron Yoe win area-round games; Lorena and Yoe meet next in an all-254 regional",
 dek:"La Vega rolled 56-7 to stay perfect, Yoe survived 50-48 and six 254 small schools also advanced Friday night. China Spring, Crawford, San Saba and Oglesby were eliminated.",
 body:[
  "La Vega beat Geronimo Navarro 56-7 Friday night at UMHB's Crusader Stadium in Belton to move to 12-0, leading a big night for 254 teams in the second round of the UIL high school football playoffs. Robinson, Lorena and Cameron Yoe also won, and the area round sets up an all-Central Texas regional game between Lorena and Yoe next week.",
  "<strong>Class 4A:</strong> La Vega's win sends the Pirates to a 4A Division II regional against unbeaten Wimberley (11-0). Robinson beat Rockport-Fulton 31-21 at Gustafson Stadium in San Antonio and will face Brownwood. Stephenville stayed unbeaten with a 38-21 win over Vidor and will play Huffman Hargrave. China Spring's run ended with a 36-12 loss to Stafford in Giddings.",
  "<strong>Class 3A:</strong> Lorena beat Diboll 50-28 in Madisonville, and Cameron Yoe edged Orangefield 50-48 in Houston. The two now meet in a 3A Division I regional. Whitney beat Tatum 40-35 Thursday and will play Gunter.",
  "<strong>Class 2A:</strong> Rosebud-Lott beat Flatonia 67-35 in Manor and will face unbeaten Shiner. Goldthwaite stayed perfect with a 70-38 win over Haskell in San Angelo and will play Santo. Crawford's season ended with a 46-23 loss to Wellington in Graham, and San Saba fell 55-3 to Muenster in Granbury. As reported earlier, Belton (5A) and Axtell (2A) were eliminated Thursday.",
  "<strong>Six-man:</strong> Aquilla beat Medina 84-72 in Priddy and Mount Calm beat Runge 53-7 in Bartlett. Aquilla, now 12-0, faces unbeaten Union Hill in the Division I regional after Union Hill beat Oglesby 100-86 in Oakwood, according to the game story and the regional bracket. One statewide scoreboard listed that score reversed. Mount Calm plays Ladonia Fannindel.",
  "Regional-round games are Nov. 26-28. Dates, times and sites were still listed as to be determined Saturday morning, and we'll post them as schools announce them. Scores come from High School Football America's statewide scoreboard, and pairings come from the statewide regional bracket. Our earlier recap of Thursday's games is <a href=\"/news/area-round-thursday-results-friday-slate/\">here</a>.",
  "Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],
 sources:[["High School Football America: area-round final scores","https://highschoolfootballamerica.com/final-scores-from-2nd-round-of-uil-texas-high-school-football-playoff-games-played-november-19-21-2026/"],["Statewide UIL regional-round pairings","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/state-wide-uil-regional-round-082321462.html"],["Union Hill vs. Oglesby game story","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/union-hill-takes-down-oglesby-063348632.html"],["KWTX: area-round pairings and sites","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"]]},
{id:"valor-prep-second-tapps-title-ctcs-falls", seo:"Valor Prep Wins Second Straight TAPPS Six-Man State Title", cat:"sports", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"summary",
 title:"Waco's Valor Prep wins second straight TAPPS six-man state title; Temple's CTCS falls in Division IV final",
 dek:"Valor beat Keller Harvest 68-44 in Robinson. Central Texas Christian finished 9-3 after a 55-22 loss to four-time champion Dallas First Baptist.",
 body:[
  "Waco's Valor Prep won its second straight TAPPS six-man Division II state championship Friday night, beating Keller Harvest Christian 68-44 at Robinson's Rocket Field, KWTX reported. The program has only played varsity football for three seasons.",
  "In the TAPPS 11-man Division IV final, also played in Waco on Friday, Temple's Central Texas Christian School lost 55-22 to Dallas First Baptist, according to the Dallas Morning News. It was First Baptist's fourth straight state title and 21st straight win.",
  "CTCS quarterback Coulter Ragsdale accounted for 291 total yards and three touchdowns, and receiver Colin Sonnier had 155 receiving yards. The Lions finished 9-3.",
  "Both titles were the last private-school championships of the fall for 254 teams. UIL playoffs continue next week with the regional round; see our <a href=\"/news/area-round-friday-la-vega-lorena-yoe-regionals/\">Friday area-round recap</a>.",
  "Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],
 sources:[["KWTX: Valor Prep wins second straight TAPPS six-man title","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/21/valor-prep-wins-second-tapps-6-man-state-championship-row/"],["Dallas Morning News via Yahoo: First Baptist wins fourth straight title","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/first-baptist-cruises-fourth-straight-032610027.html"],["KWTX: title-game pairings and site","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/area-rounds-private-school-title-games-this-weeks-2026-central-texas-hsfb-playoff-pairings/"]]},
{id:"clifton-state-volleyball-title-salado-runner-up", seo:"Clifton Wins First State Volleyball Title; Salado Runner-Up", cat:"sports", city:"Clifton", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"records",
 title:"Clifton sweeps Wall for its first state volleyball title; Salado finishes as 4A state runner-up",
 dek:"The Cubs won 25-21, 25-23, 25-19 in Garland. Salado fell in three close sets to Decatur in the 4A Division I final.",
 body:[
  "Clifton won the UIL Class 3A Division II state volleyball championship Friday in Garland, sweeping Wall 25-21, 25-23, 25-19 at the Curtis Culwell Center, according to the UIL's official state tournament results. KWTX reported it is the Bosque County school's first state title in any team sport, and that Taliyha Davenport was named MVP.",
  "Clifton came into the final 43-4, according to the UIL bracket, and finished 44-4.",
  "Salado reached the 4A Division I final but lost to Decatur 25-23, 25-21, 25-21. The Eagles entered the match 44-6, the UIL listing shows, and finish as state runner-up.",
  "Volleyball is now done for the fall. High school basketball is underway, and soccer starts in January.",
  "Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],
 sources:[["UIL state volleyball tournament results","https://www.uiltexas.org/volleyball/state","record"],["KWTX: Clifton wins 3A-II state volleyball title","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/20/clifton-wins-3a-2-state-volleyball-title/"],["Sports Illustrated High School: set scores","https://www.si.com/high-school/texas/texas-high-school-volleyball-uil-state-championship-schedule-nov-19-21-202-01m7ek9qfzsc"]]},
{id:"mars-waco-107-million-utility-building", seo:"Mars Plans $107 Million Building at Waco Candy Plant", cat:"business", top:1, city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"records",
 title:"Mars files plans for a $107 million building at its Waco candy plant",
 dek:"A state construction filing shows a new 28,154-square-foot central utility building on Texas Central Parkway, with work set for January 2027 through February 2029.",
 body:[
  "Mars Snackfood US has filed plans for a $107 million central utility building at its candy plant at 1001 Texas Central Parkway in Waco, according to a state construction filing registered Nov. 6 with the Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation.",
  "The McLennan County filing describes a new one-story building on an undeveloped part of the existing plant property that will hold new mechanical equipment. It lists 28,154 square feet and an estimated cost of $107,022,000. The project name on the filing is \"Mars Snacking Refrigeration Replacement.\"",
  "Construction is scheduled to start Jan. 16, 2027, and finish Feb. 28, 2029. The design firm is BRR Architecture of Overland Park, Kansas. The filing lists the project as privately funded, and its state accessibility review is complete.",
  "The filing does not say whether the project will add jobs.",
  "Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],
 sources:[["TDLR filing TABS2027005354","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027005354","record"]]},
{id:"bell-county-filings-belton-warehouse-killeen-fire-station", seo:"Belton Warehouse Park, Killeen Fire Station in State Filings", cat:"growth", city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"records", also:["real-estate"],
 title:"$24 million warehouse park in Belton, new Killeen fire station and credit union branch show up in state filings",
 dek:"Three Bell County projects worth $33.5 million were registered with the state this month, with construction set to start in 2027.",
 body:[
  "A $24 million, three-building warehouse park in Belton leads a group of new Bell County construction projects registered with the state this month, including a $7 million Killeen fire station and a $2.5 million credit union branch, according to Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation filings.",
  "<strong>Belton warehouse park:</strong> DBI San Marcos Property LP filed plans Nov. 11 for the DBI Capitol Way Warehouse Development at 815 Elm Grove Spur and 3015 Capitol Way Drive. The filing describes three shell buildings with warehouse and office suites totaling 180,960 square feet, with construction from Feb. 1, 2027, to May 15, 2028.",
  "<strong>Killeen Fire Station 5:</strong> A new 11,293-square-foot fire station at 202 W. Jasper Drive was registered Nov. 18 with an estimated cost of $7 million. The publicly funded project is scheduled from May 1, 2027, to May 1, 2028.",
  "<strong>A+ Federal Credit Union:</strong> The Austin-based credit union registered a new 3,200-square-foot branch at 510 W. Stan Schlueter Loop in Killeen on Nov. 16. It is estimated at $2.5 million, with work from Feb. 1 to Dec. 1, 2027.",
  "State filings are early steps. Plans and dates can change before construction starts. More projects are on our <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a> tracker, including the Bell County <a href=\"/news/bell-county-justice-center-annex-price/\">Justice Center Annex</a>.",
  "Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],
 sources:[["TDLR filing TABS2027005693 (Belton warehouses)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027005693","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2027006136 (Killeen Fire Station 5)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027006136","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2027005951 (A+ FCU Killeen)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027005951","record"],["Killeen Daily Herald: A+ FCU plans Killeen branch","https://kdhnews.com/business/a-federal-credit-union-plans-2-5-million-killeen-branch/article_c1254620-cef1-4242-8453-22ea6efeff6b.html"]]},
{id:"laynes-waco-di-campli-mcgregor-fairfield-gatesville", seo:"Layne's to Waco, Di Campli's to McGregor, Gatesville Fairfield", cat:"business", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"records",
 title:"Layne's Chicken Fingers coming to Waco, Di Campli's heads to McGregor and a Gatesville hotel becomes a Fairfield Inn",
 dek:"State filings show a former Fazoli's on South Sixth Street being remodeled for Layne's, a restaurant in McGregor's old bank building and a Marriott conversion on SH 36.",
 body:[
  "Layne's Chicken Fingers plans a Waco restaurant at 919 S. 6th St., the current Fazoli's building near Baylor, according to a state construction filing registered Nov. 17. The filing lists a $300,000 remodel of the 2,829-square-foot drive-thru restaurant, with work from Feb. 8 to June 28, 2027. What Now Dallas first reported the plans and identified the local franchisee; no opening date has been announced.",
  "<strong>McGregor:</strong> Di Campli's Italian Ristorante, now on Woodway Drive in Waco, has filed plans for 222 Main St. in McGregor, inside the historic First National Bank Building. The Nov. 3 filing lists a $420,000 renovation of 3,750 square feet of vacant space with a new covered patio, scheduled from Dec. 1, 2026, to Dec. 1, 2027. The filing does not say whether the Waco location will stay open.",
  "<strong>Gatesville:</strong> An existing hotel at 111 State Highway 36 is set to be renovated and converted to a Fairfield Inn & Suites by Marriott, according to a Nov. 11 filing. The $1 million project covers new furniture, carpet and bathrooms across 36,784 square feet, from Jan. 15 to Sept. 15, 2027.",
  "See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],
 sources:[["TDLR filing TABS2027006049 (Layne's, Waco)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027006049","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2027005055 (Di Campli's, McGregor)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027005055","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2027005689 (Fairfield Inn, Gatesville)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2027005689","record"],["What Now: Layne's planning Waco site","https://whatnow.com/dallas/restaurants/laynes-chicken-fingers-planning-new-waco-site/"]]},
{id:"altair-clear-creek-killeen-apartments-rents", seo:"Altair at Clear Creek Killeen Apartments: Units and Rents", cat:"real-estate", city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"summary",
 title:"New Killeen apartments at Altair at Clear Creek: 182 units, one-bedrooms from about $1,444",
 dek:"The $27 million complex on Clear Creek Road is nearing completion, with two- and three-bedroom units listed at about $1,864 and $2,078.",
 body:[
  "Altair at Clear Creek, a 182-unit apartment complex at 3904 Clear Creek Road in Killeen, is nearing completion, with one-bedroom rents starting around $1,444 a month, the Killeen Daily Herald reported Nov. 20.",
  "The complex has 19 two-story buildings on about 10.2 acres. Two-bedroom units are listed at about $1,864 and three-bedrooms at about $2,078. Those figures include required monthly fees but not utilities, the Herald reported.",
  "The city listed the project as 70% complete in its second-quarter 2026 report, and construction is now scheduled to wrap up in March 2027, according to the Herald.",
  "The original state construction filing, registered in 2024 by OG Central Texas Partners Apts, lists the project at $27 million with a garden-style layout, a clubhouse, pool and mail kiosk. That filing had targeted completion in August 2026, so the project is running later than first planned.",
  "Track home prices and rates on our <a href=\"/real-estate/#housing-dashboard\">254 Housing Dashboard</a>. This is general information, not financial advice."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: $27M apartment development nearing completion","https://kdhnews.com/business/27m-apartment-development-nearing-completion-in-killeen-1-444-for-a-one-bedroom/article_905ba03d-ec3b-45df-ac7f-40daaed25011.html"],["TDLR filing TABS2025001582 (Altair at Clear Creek)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Search/Project/TABS2025001582","record"]]},
{id:"bell-county-killeen-annex-opening-nov-30", seo:"Bell County Killeen Annex Opens Nov. 30: What You Can Do", cat:"government", city:"Killeen", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"summary",
 title:"Bell County opens its new downtown Killeen annex Nov. 30: what you can do there",
 dek:"Vehicle registration, the appraisal district, veterans services and a justice of the peace court move into 507 N. Gray St. Early voting in the Dec. 12 runoffs starts the same day.",
 body:[
  "Bell County will hold a public opening ceremony for its new Killeen annex at 2 p.m. Monday, Nov. 30, at 507 N. Gray St. in downtown Killeen, the Killeen Daily Herald reported. Precinct 4 Commissioner Louie Minor is hosting, and the event is free and open to the public.",
  "The annex houses the Precinct 4 justice of the peace and constable, vehicle registration, the appraisal district, the Veterans Service Office and the county treasurer, according to the Herald. The building brings those county offices together in downtown Killeen.",
  "The same day, Nov. 30, early voting begins for Texas' Dec. 12 runoff elections and runs through Dec. 8, according to the Texas Secretary of State's election calendar. The deadline to apply for a mail ballot is Dec. 1. Voter registration for the runoff has already closed. Our explainer on the Bell County Appraisal District board race on that ballot is <a href=\"/news/we-the-people-bellcad-runoff/\">here</a>."],
 sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: Bell County to celebrate opening of new annex","https://kdhnews.com/business/bell-county-to-celebrate-opening-of-new-annex-in-killeen/article_2d4a352f-dac1-41d8-b56d-92c406bb6db6.html"],["Texas Secretary of State: Dec. 12, 2026 runoff election calendar","https://www.sos.state.tx.us/elections/laws/advisory2026-27-dec-12-runoff-election-law-calendar.shtml","record"]]},
{id:"baylor-hrsa-grant-behavioral-health-social-work", seo:"Baylor Gets $2.2M Grant for Behavioral Health Social Workers", cat:"education", city:"Waco", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"records",
 title:"Baylor gets $2.2 million federal grant to train more behavioral health social workers",
 dek:"The four-year grant pays $25,000 stipends to 14 master's students a year who train in clinics including Baylor Scott & White, Temple Community Clinic and Waco Family Medicine.",
 body:[
  "Baylor University's Diana R. Garland School of Social Work in Waco has received a four-year, $2.2 million federal grant to train social workers for behavioral health jobs in clinics and hospitals, especially in rural and underserved areas, the university announced Nov. 18.",
  "The Health Resources and Services Administration grant funds Baylor's Integrated Behavioral Health Certificate Program. Each year, 14 advanced Master of Social Work students will get a $25,000 stipend and complete internships in integrated care settings such as community health centers.",
  "Baylor said 246 of Texas' 254 counties qualify as behavioral health professional shortage areas, and about 90% of Garland School graduates stay in Texas. Partners include Baylor Scott & White, Temple Community Clinic, the Texas Association of Community Health Centers and Waco Family Medicine.",
  "The program also offers free continuing education for behavioral health workers already on the job at partner organizations. Program lead Becky Bell Scott said more than half of the grant money goes directly to students, which means less borrowing for their degrees."],
 sources:[["Baylor University news release, Nov. 18, 2026","https://news.web.baylor.edu/news/story/2026/federal-grant-address-critical-workforce-need-behavioral-health-professionals-texas","record"]]},
{id:"thanksgiving-weekend-254-2026", seo:"Thanksgiving Weekend in the 254: Events and Holiday Markets", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-21", basis:"summary",
 title:"Thanksgiving weekend in the 254: Homestead Fair, Wild Lights, Temple's tree lighting and a Belton holiday market",
 dek:"A turkey trot in Waco, holiday lights opening across the area and Black Friday shopping that isn't at the mall. Here's the plan for Nov. 26-29.",
 body:[
  "Thanksgiving weekend kicks off the holiday season across Central Texas, with lights, markets and shows in Waco, Temple, Belton and Salado from Thursday, Nov. 26, through Sunday, Nov. 29.",
  "<strong>Thursday, Nov. 26:</strong> Burn off the pie early at Waco's Poultry in Motion Turkey Trot at Indian Spring Park, with a 1K at 8 a.m. and a 5K at 8:30 a.m. benefiting the Community Cancer Association.",
  "<strong>Friday, Nov. 27:</strong> Several big holiday traditions open. The Homestead Fair at Homestead Heritage near Waco runs through Sunday with farm animals, craft demonstrations and scratch-made food, and admission is free. Christmas at the Silos begins at Magnolia, Wild Lights opens at Cameron Park Zoo and Waco Civic Theatre opens <em>Annie</em>, which runs through Dec. 20. In Belton, the Merry Mistletoe Marketplace holiday craft show runs Friday through Sunday at the Expo Center on West Loop 121; adults are $8 and kids 12 and under get in free.",
  "<strong>Saturday, Nov. 28:</strong> Temple's Christmas at the Plaza runs 2 to 8 p.m. at Santa Fe Plaza with live reindeer and a kids' zone, and the tree lighting is at 7:30 p.m., according to the City of Temple. For a night out in Waco, The Reverend Horton Heat plays The Backyard. It's also Small Business Saturday, a good day to shop downtown Belton, Salado's Main Street and downtown Waco.",
  "Every event, with times and filters for kids, date night and free, is on our <a href=\"/things-to-do/\">Things to Do guide</a>. Dates come from event organizers and venue listings; check with the venue before you go."],
 sources:[["Downtown Waco: Turkey Trot","https://downtownwacotx.com/events/waco-turkey-trot/"],["Homestead Fair","https://www.homesteadfair.com/"],["Magnolia: Christmas at the Silos","https://magnolia.com/visit/events/christmas-at-the-silos"],["City of Temple: Holly Jolly and Christmas at the Plaza","https://city-of-temple.prowly.com/467925-city-of-temple-announces-return-of-holly-jolly-month-long-holiday-celebration"],["Merry Mistletoe Marketplace tickets","https://www.tickettailor.com/events/samishow/2075031"],["Waco Civic Theatre: Annie","https://ctxlivetheatre.com/productions/20261127-annie-the-musical-by-waco-civic-theatre/"],["The Backyard: Reverend Horton Heat","https://www.etix.com/ticket/p/90313876"]]},
{"id": "wine-basics-what-dry-means", "cat": "things-to-do", "city": "Central Texas", "date": "2026-11-22", "author": "jake-ruse", "basis": "original", "title": "Wine Basics: What 'Dry' Actually Means", "dek": "Dry wine means the yeast ate almost all the grape sugar. Here's where the line really sits, and why fruity is not the same as sweet.", "body": ["Short answer: a dry wine is one where the yeast finished the job and ate nearly all the grape sugar, so there's little or none left for you to taste.", "Every wine starts as sweet grape juice. During fermentation, yeast turns that sugar into alcohol and carbon dioxide. Whatever sugar is left when fermentation stops is residual sugar, or RS, measured in grams per liter. No wine gets all the way to zero. A small share of grape sugars are ones wine yeast can't ferment, so even a bone-dry wine usually sits around 1 to 2 grams per liter.", "So where's the line? European label law is the cleanest yardstick: a still wine can say dry with up to 4 grams per liter, or up to 9 if the acidity is high enough to balance it. Medium dry runs up to 12, medium sweet up to 45, and anything above that is sweet. Here's what the label won't tell you: plenty of big-brand reds sold as \"smooth\" carry several grams of sugar to round them out, and most U.S. wine labels don't list sugar at all.", "This is the most common mix-up in wine: dry is not the opposite of fruity. A Zinfandel that smells like blackberry jam can be completely dry. Your nose picks up ripe fruit, vanilla from oak or flowers, and your brain fills in the word \"sweet.\" Aromatic grapes like Muscat, Gewurztraminer and Riesling fool people constantly, even when the wine in the glass is bone dry.", "Structure pulls the other way. Acidity and tannin, the grippy texture in a young Cabernet that dries out your gums, both make a wine taste less sweet than it really is. That's why a Riesling with real sugar can still taste crisp and balanced, and why some makers of high-acid whites leave a gram or two in on purpose to take the edge off. Temperature plays in too: a warm red tastes sweeter, heavier and hotter than the same wine served a few degrees cooler.", "My advice: when you ask for \"dry,\" say what you're actually trying to avoid. \"Nothing sweet\" and \"nothing that dries my mouth out\" are two different requests, and the second one is about tannin, not sugar. Tell your server or wine shop which one you mean and they'll hand you the right bottle.", "Takeaway: dry means low sugar, not low flavor. Trust your tongue over the word on the label.", "More from Jake: <a href=\"/sip-the-254/\">Sip the 254</a>."], "sources": [["EU Regulation 2019/33 (wine labeling, sweetness terms in Annex III)", "https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg_del/2019/33/oj", "record"], ["Decanter: What is residual sugar in wine?", "https://www.decanter.com/learn/residual-sugar-46007/"]]},
{id:"hike-layering-cold-front", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-22", trail:"gear", basis:"original",
 title:"Pack & Weather: How to layer for a Central Texas cold front",
 dek:"A cold front can turn a mild hike into a cold, windy one. Here's how to layer so you stay dry, warm and comfortable on the trail.",
 body:[
  "Short answer: wear three layers you can take off and put back on. A base layer that moves sweat off your skin, a warm middle layer and a shell that blocks wind and rain. Skip cotton. Pack the layer you think you won't need.",
  "<strong>Why it matters here:</strong> Central Texas fall and winter hikes often start in one kind of weather and end in another. Check the National Weather Service forecast for your trail before you leave, and look at the wind, not just the temperature.",
  "<strong>The base layer:</strong> REI says this layer's job is wicking, moving perspiration away from your skin. Wool or synthetic fabrics do that. REI calls cotton a no-no in cold weather because it soaks up water and can chill you. The U.S. Forest Service says inner layers should be wool or synthetics that stay warm when wet.",
  "<strong>The middle layer:</strong> this one holds in body heat. A fleece or a light puffy jacket works. REI's advice is to add it if hiking alone isn't keeping you warm.",
  "<strong>The outer layer:</strong> a shell shields you from wind and rain. It matters most on exposed ground. The Waco Lake Dam Hike & Bike Trail has little shade and wide-open lake views, so a north wind there hits you with nothing in the way.",
  "<strong>Adjust before you get wet:</strong> the Forest Service says that as you get hot and sweat, you can shed a layer or two and stay comfortable. Climbs make that matter. Cameron Park in Waco has short, steep climbs and lots of shade, so you can heat up on the way up and cool off fast once you stop. Take a layer off at the bottom of a climb and put it back on at the top. REI puts it simply: you can peel off layers if things heat up, but you can't put on layers you didn't bring.",
  "<strong>Know the danger signs:</strong> the National Weather Service says hypothermia can happen in temperatures as warm as 60 degrees, especially in water or when you're outside a long time and not dressed for the weather. The Forest Service says it can happen above 40 degrees when someone gets chilled from rain, sweat or cold water. Watch for uncontrollable shivering, confusion, drowsiness and loss of coordination. The NWS says to act at the first sign, and to call for emergency help if you suspect hypothermia.",
  "<strong>Your pack list for a front:</strong> base layer on, middle layer and shell in the pack, a hat and light gloves, a dry spare shirt for the car, water and a snack. You still need water when it's cold.",
  "<strong>Before you drive out:</strong> check trail status. Texas Parks and Wildlife says the south gate at Mother Neff State Park is closed, and flood damage along the Leon River is still being repaired. Dana Peak Park in Harker Heights is closed October through March.",
  "More: <a href=\"/trails/\">Trails & Hiking in the 254</a>."],
 sources:[["REI Expert Advice: Layering Basics","https://www.rei.com/learn/expert-advice/layering-basics"],["National Weather Service: During Extremely Cold Weather","https://www.weather.gov/safety/cold-during","record"],["U.S. Forest Service: Hypothermia","https://www.fs.usda.gov/visit/know-before-you-go/hypothermia","record"],["Texas Parks and Wildlife: Mother Neff State Park alerts","https://tpwd.texas.gov/state-parks/mother-neff/alert","record"]]},
{id:"baylor-falls-texas-tech-20-10-senior-day",cat:"sports",top:1,city:"Waco",date:"2026-11-22",basis:"summary",title:"Baylor falls 20-10 to No. 12 Texas Tech on Senior Day in Waco",dek:"The Bears (6-5) were tied at halftime at McLane Stadium but managed 31 rushing yards and now close the season at Houston.",body:["Baylor lost its final home game of 2026 on Saturday, Nov. 21, falling 20-10 to No. 12 Texas Tech at McLane Stadium in Waco, according to KWKT (FOX 44). The game was tied at halftime before the Red Raiders pulled away.","<strong>How it got away:</strong> Texas Tech outgained Baylor 402 to 267 and ran for 231 yards to the Bears' 31. Red Raiders quarterback Lagway completed 30 of 48 passes for 236 yards and a touchdown.","<strong>Bright spots for Baylor:</strong> the defense forced three turnovers, with interceptions by Ryan Davis and LeVar Thornton Jr. and a forced fumble, and added nine tackles for loss and two sacks. Gavin Freeman caught six passes, his 16th straight game with at least five. Punter Palmer Williams boomed an 81-yarder, the longest Baylor punt in 46 years, KWKT reported.","<strong>Where Baylor stands:</strong> the loss drops the Bears to 6-5 overall and 4-4 in the Big 12. They came into the day at 6-4 (<a href=\"/news/baylor-football-texas-tech-senior-day/\">our preview</a>).","<strong>What's next:</strong> Baylor closes the regular season at No. 21 Houston on Saturday, Nov. 28, at 8:30 p.m. on ESPN2.","Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],sources:[["KWKT (FOX 44): Baylor comes up short in final home game","https://www.fox44news.com/sports/baylor/baylor-comes-up-short-in-final-home-game-falling-20-10-to-no-12-texas-tech/"],["Baylor Athletics: Houston kickoff time","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/11/16/football-baylor-at-houston-set-for-8-30-pm-on-espn2","record"]]},
{id:"tarleton-state-12-0-uac-title-north-alabama",seo:"Tarleton State Finishes 12-0, Wins Outright UAC Title",cat:"sports",top:1,city:"Stephenville",date:"2026-11-22",basis:"records",title:"Tarleton State finishes 12-0, wins outright UAC title at North Alabama",dek:"The Stephenville Texans beat North Alabama 31-24 to complete a perfect regular season and learn their FCS playoff seed Sunday.",body:["Tarleton State football finished the regular season unbeaten on Saturday, Nov. 21, beating North Alabama 31-24 in Florence, Ala., to go 12-0 and clinch the outright United Athletic Conference championship, according to Tarleton Athletics. The Texans went 7-0 in conference play.","It is the fourth undefeated regular season in program history for the Stephenville school, and Tarleton Athletics said the Texans are one of only two Division I football teams still without a loss.","<strong>The stars:</strong> quarterback Kaden Anderson threw for 299 yards and two touchdowns. Tylan Hines ran for 143 yards and two scores, Miequle Brock added 109 rushing yards, and Tanner Schmidt caught 11 passes for 149 yards and a touchdown. Tarleton outgained North Alabama 561 to 364 and recorded four sacks.","<strong>What's next:</strong> the FCS playoff field is revealed Sunday, Nov. 22, in an 11 a.m. selection show on ESPNU. Tarleton is hosting a watch party at the EECU Center in Stephenville, with doors at 10:30 a.m. As the UAC champion, Tarleton holds the league's automatic bid, NCAA.com reported. The Texans entered the week ranked No. 1 in the FCS (<a href=\"/news/tarleton-state-no1-fcs/\">earlier coverage</a>).","Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],sources:[["Tarleton Athletics: game recap","https://tarletonsports.com/news/2026/11/21/perfect-tarleton-state-football-posts-undefeated-regular-season-clinches-outright-uac-championship-with-win-at-north-alabama.aspx","record"],["ESPN: Tarleton State 31, North Alabama 24","https://www.espn.com/college-football/game/_/gameId/401868234"],["NCAA.com: FCS automatic bid tracker","https://www.ncaa.com/news/football/article/2026-11-21/2026-fcs-playoffs-automatic-bid-tracker-and-scenarios"]]},
{id:"mclennan-county-general-fund-5-5-million-drawdown",seo:"McLennan County Expects $5.5M General Fund Drawdown",cat:"government",city:"Waco",date:"2026-11-22",basis:"summary",title:"McLennan County expects to spend $5.5 million more than it takes in this year",dek:"A McLennan County budget workshop projected the general fund falling to just under $46 million, with no vote taken.",body:["McLennan County expects to spend about $5.5 million more than it collects this fiscal year, leaving its general fund balance just under $46 million, KWTX reported from a Nov. 17 budget workshop at the county in Waco.","<strong>The numbers:</strong> projections for fiscal 2027 show about $159 million in revenue against nearly $165 million in spending. County Auditor Frances Bartlett said the drop would have been close to $17 million without this year's 4-cent property tax rate increase, according to KWTX.","<strong>The cushion:</strong> the county aims to keep reserves at 28% to 33% of operating costs. If departments finish the year 3% under budget, the balance could land near $51 million. Officials are also tracking about $10 million in spending that has been put off.","County Judge Scott Felton pointed to the cost of holding inmates who are waiting on state transfer, which runs about $100 to $115 a day per person, KWTX reported.","<strong>What happens next:</strong> this was a workshop, so commissioners took no action. Officials said it was meant to bring incoming court members up to speed before work starts on the fiscal 2028 budget."],sources:[["KWTX: McLennan County projects $5.5 million decrease in general fund","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/18/mclennan-county-projects-55-million-decrease-general-fund-balance/"]]},
{id:"killeen-council-gonzalez-resigns-district-1",seo:"Killeen District 1 Council Seat to Be Filled by Appointment",cat:"government",city:"Killeen",date:"2026-11-22",basis:"summary",title:"Killeen Mayor Pro Tem Jessica Gonzalez resigns; council will appoint District 1 replacement",dek:"Gonzalez, elected a Bell County justice of the peace, will stay on the Killeen City Council until the council appoints her successor.",body:["Killeen Mayor Pro Tem Jessica Gonzalez turned in her resignation from the District 1 City Council seat on Nov. 18 and plans to keep serving until a replacement is appointed, the Killeen Daily Herald reported.","<strong>Why she is leaving:</strong> Gonzalez won the Nov. 3 election for Bell County Justice of the Peace, Precinct 4, Place 2. That term begins Jan. 1, 2027.","<strong>How the seat gets filled:</strong> under the city charter, the council will appoint a District 1 resident by majority vote to serve through November 2027. City Attorney Holli Clements said no special election is needed, according to the Herald.","Residents will have a two-week window to apply through the city secretary's office. The council voted 7-0 for staff to bring back proposed dates for applications, interviews and the appointment. Those dates had not been announced as of Nov. 22."],sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: Gonzalez turns in resignation","https://kdhnews.com/government/gonzalez-turns-in-resignation-intends-to-stay-on-killeen-council-until-replacement-selected/article_0263ac4c-1ad0-4cf3-af25-ef6c69f315eb.html"]]},
{id:"copperas-cove-place-7-runoff-withdrawal",seo:"Copperas Cove Place 7 Runoff Off After Candidate Withdraws",cat:"government",city:"Copperas Cove",date:"2026-11-22",basis:"summary",title:"Copperas Cove council Place 7 runoff off after candidate withdraws; Dana Wall to take seat",dek:"Trae Cunningham withdrew from the Dec. 12 Copperas Cove runoff, and the council is expected to cancel that race Nov. 24.",body:["Trae Cunningham withdrew on Nov. 18 from the Copperas Cove City Council Place 7 runoff, leaving Dana Wall as the winner in effect, the Copperas Cove Herald reported. Wall said Cunningham stepped aside to focus on his hospice work.","<strong>What happens next:</strong> the City Council is expected to accept the withdrawal on Nov. 24 and cancel the Place 7 runoff that had been set for Dec. 12.","<strong>Still on the ballot:</strong> the Place 6 runoff between Jay Manning and Jesus Mendez is still scheduled.","The withdrawal came a day after the election canvass. Had it come before the canvass, third-place finisher William Smith would have moved into the runoff against Wall, according to the Herald."],sources:[["Copperas Cove Herald (KDH): Place 7 seat set after candidate withdraws","https://kdhnews.com/copperas_cove_herald/cove-council-place-7-seat-set-after-candidate-withdraws/article_b44b22a4-e9cc-4375-abeb-f9a29dccbe6e.html"]]},
{id:"temple-fire-station-9-old-waco-road",seo:"Temple Plans $19M Fire Station 9 on Old Waco Road",cat:"growth",city:"Temple",date:"2026-11-22",basis:"summary",title:"Temple plans $19 million-plus Fire Station 9 on Old Waco Road as two stations get renovated",dek:"Temple's fire chief outlined a 26,000-square-foot Station 9 and 2027 finish dates for renovations at Stations 2 and 4.",body:["Temple plans to build Fire Station 9 on Old Waco Road at an estimated cost of more than $19 million, Fire Chief Christopher Perez told the Temple Rotary Club, the Temple Daily Telegram reported Nov. 21. The station in Bell County would be about 26,000 square feet and take about 18 months to build.","<strong>Renovations underway:</strong> Fire Station 2 at 1710 E. Avenue H and Fire Station 4 at 411 Waters Dairy Road are each getting a $1.5 million renovation and addition, according to state construction filings. The filings list completion dates of Jan. 1, 2027, for Station 2 and June 1, 2027, for Station 4.","<strong>Also on the way:</strong> a separate state filing shows a new $7.8 million, 12,000-square-foot Fire Station No. 7 at 10354 W. Adams Ave., with work scheduled from September 2026 to October 2027.","<strong>Trucks and schedules:</strong> Perez said a fire engine costs about $1 million and typically lasts about 15 years. He is also considering a one-year trial starting Jan. 1 of a 48-hours-on, 96-hours-off shift, replacing the current 24-on, 48-off schedule, the Telegram reported.","We did not find a state construction filing for Station 9 yet; the cost and size come from the chief's remarks as reported by the Telegram.","Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],sources:[["Temple Daily Telegram: Temple fire chief shares news about stations, costs","https://www.tdtnews.com/news/central_texas_news/article_1d8d06ca-2b69-44ab-a12a-fbee5da650a9.html"],["TDLR filing TABS2026009813 (Fire Station 2)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Projects/TABS2026009813","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2026016269 (Fire Station 4)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Projects/TABS2026016269","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2026020229 (Fire Station No. 7)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Projects/TABS2026020229","record"]]},
{id:"mcc-foundation-record-925k-scholarships",cat:"education",city:"Waco",date:"2026-11-22",basis:"summary",title:"MCC Foundation awards a record $925,069 in scholarships",dek:"McLennan Community College's foundation in Waco gave 683 awards for 2026-27, its most in 36 years; 2027-28 applications are due Jan. 15.",body:["The McLennan Community College Foundation in Waco awarded a record $925,069 in scholarships for the 2026-27 school year, the most in its 36-year history, KXXV reported Nov. 20.","<strong>By the numbers:</strong> the foundation made 683 awards, up almost 9% from last year. It also processed 383 emergency grant applications, adding about $208,000 in aid for students.","<strong>Honorees:</strong> the foundation gave its Distinguished Alumni Award to Michael Olmstead, a 2002 MCC graduate who is chief operating officer of Buckner Retirement Services, and its Distinguished Leader Award to Yuto Goto. Chris Qualls is the foundation's executive director.","<strong>For students:</strong> the priority deadline for 2027-28 MCC Foundation scholarship applications is Jan. 15, 2027, through the college's AwardSpring portal."],sources:[["KXXV: MCC Foundation awards record $925K in student scholarships","https://www.kxxv.com/news/local-news/in-your-neighborhood/mclennan-county/mcc-foundation-awards-record-925k-in-student-scholarships"],["MCC scholarship portal","https://mclennan.awardspring.com/"]]},
{id:"china-spring-isd-leslie-smith-superintendent-finalist",seo:"China Spring ISD Names Leslie Smith Superintendent Finalist",cat:"education",city:"China Spring",date:"2026-11-22",basis:"summary",title:"China Spring ISD names Dr. Leslie Smith lone finalist for superintendent",dek:"The McLennan County district's deputy superintendent was picked Nov. 16; state law requires a 21-day wait before the board can hire her.",body:["The China Spring ISD board of trustees named Dr. Leslie Smith the lone finalist for superintendent on Nov. 16, KWTX reported, citing a district release. China Spring ISD serves families northwest of Waco in McLennan County.","<strong>Who she is:</strong> Smith has 20 years in education, 10 of them at China Spring ISD, where she is deputy superintendent of leadership. She has also served the district as curriculum director, executive director of human resources and assistant superintendent, and earlier worked in Midway ISD.","She holds degrees from Abilene Christian University, the University of Texas at Tyler and Tarleton State University, where she earned her doctorate.","<strong>What happens next:</strong> Texas law requires a 21-day waiting period after a lone finalist is named before the board can vote to hire. That puts the earliest possible vote in early December; the district had not announced a date."],sources:[["KWTX: China Spring ISD names Dr. Leslie Smith lone finalist","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/17/china-spring-isd-names-dr-leslie-smith-lone-finalist-superintendent/"]]},
{id:"nola-soul-seafood-opens-killeen",cat:"business",city:"Killeen",date:"2026-11-22",basis:"summary",title:"NOLA Soul & Seafood opens in north Killeen",dek:"New Orleans natives opened the Cajun seafood restaurant at 615 N. Second St. in Killeen, serving po'boys and scratch-made sides.",body:["NOLA Soul & Seafood opened the week of Nov. 17 at 615 N. Second St. in Killeen, the Killeen Daily Herald reported. The restaurant is run by New Orleans natives Timothy N. and Shantalyn W. through their company, Who Dat Soul & Seafood Corp.","<strong>On the menu:</strong> New Orleans-style seafood and soul food, including catfish po'boys and sides made from scratch.","<strong>Hours:</strong> 11 a.m. to 6 p.m., Tuesday through Sunday. The phone number is 254-213-0860.","It joins a run of new openings in Killeen this fall, including the <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/chick-fil-a-south-killeen/\">south Killeen Chick-fil-A</a>.","See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],sources:[["Killeen Daily Herald: New seafood restaurant opens its doors in Killeen","https://kdhnews.com/business/new-seafood-restaurant-opens-its-doors-in-killeen/article_478b87ab-454d-41ec-b311-24e1ad1eb283.html"]]},
{id:"tarleton-texas-am-soarr-rural-student-grant",seo:"Tarleton Gets $2.1M Share of $4.4M Rural Student Grant",cat:"education",city:"Stephenville",date:"2026-11-22",basis:"records",title:"Tarleton State gets $2.1 million share of $4.4 million federal grant for rural students",dek:"The five-year SOARR grant with Texas A&M will fund a Stephenville summer program, mentoring and paid work for first-generation and rural students.",body:["Tarleton State University in Stephenville will receive $2,108,768 of a five-year, $4.4 million U.S. Department of Education grant shared with Texas A&M, according to a Tarleton news release.","<strong>Who it helps:</strong> the program, called SOARR, targets first-generation, low-income and rural students returning as sophomores or transferring in as juniors.","<strong>What it pays for:</strong> a 14-day residential summer program in Stephenville, with a matching program in College Station, plus peer mentoring, paid work-based learning, credentials and entrepreneurship training.","The grant comes from the federal Strengthening Institutions Program and was awarded to Texas A&M. Tarleton's Center for Rural Resilience will run its part, with Dr. Subi Gandhi and Dr. Jean Lonie Dudley as co-investigators."],sources:[["Tarleton State University news release","https://www.tarleton.edu/news/4-4-million-soarr-grant-unites-tarleton-state-texas-am-to-advance-rural-student-success/","record"]]},
{"id":"regional-round-254-teams-times-sites-nov-27","seo":"Regional Round Playoff Guide: 254 Teams, Times, Sites","cat":"sports","city":"Central Texas","date":"2026-11-23","top":1,"title":"Regional round guide: 11 teams from the 254 play Friday, with times and sites","dek":"La Vega, Robinson, Stephenville, Lorena, Cameron Yoe, Bremond and more play UIL regional games Friday, Nov. 27. Here are kickoff times and stadiums.","body":["Eleven Central Texas football teams are still alive in the UIL playoffs, and all of them play regional-round games on Friday, Nov. 27, according to the regional slate posted by KWTX and game sites listed by Dave Campbell's Texas Football.","<strong>The all-254 game:</strong> Lorena (10-2) and Cameron Yoe (11-1) meet in Class 3A Division I at Salado ISD Stadium. KWTX lists kickoff at 7:30 p.m. and Dave Campbell's lists 7 p.m., so check with either school before you leave. Lorena beat Diboll 50-28 in the area round, and Yoe outlasted Orangefield 50-48.","<strong>Class 4A:</strong> Unbeaten La Vega (12-0) plays unbeaten Wimberley (11-0) at 7 p.m. at The Pfield in Pflugerville after routing Geronimo Navarro 56-7. Robinson (10-2) faces Brownwood (7-5) at 7 p.m. at Wildcat Stadium in Godley after beating Rockport-Fulton 31-21. Stephenville (12-0) beat Vidor 38-21 and now plays Bay City (11-1) at 2 p.m. at Hutto Memorial Stadium, according to Dave Campbell's.","<strong>Class 3A and 2A:</strong> Whitney (11-1) plays Gunter (11-1) at 1 p.m. at Pennington Field in Bedford. Rosebud-Lott (11-1) faces unbeaten Shiner at 3 p.m. at House Park in Austin. Bremond (12-0), a 71-21 winner over Three Rivers, plays Junction at 7 p.m. at Gupton Stadium in Cedar Park. Goldthwaite (12-0) plays Santo at 7 p.m. at Cervetto Stadium in Dublin.","<strong>Six-man:</strong> Aquilla (12-0) plays unbeaten Union Hill at 7 p.m. in Division I; the site had not been posted by KWTX as of Monday. Mount Calm (11-1) plays Ladonia Fannindel at 7 p.m. at the Coolidge athletic complex in Division II.","Earlier this postseason, Waco's Valor Prep won the TAPPS six-man Division II title. Read more: <a href=\"/news/valor-prep-second-tapps-title-ctcs-falls/\">Valor Prep wins second straight state title</a>.","Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],"sources":[["KWTX: UIL regional round slate","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/23/uil-regional-round-check-out-this-weeks-central-txhsfb-playoff-slate/"],["Dave Campbell's Texas Football: playoff game times and locations","https://www.davecampbells.com/articles/2026/11/07/txhsfb-playoffs-game-times-and-locations"]]},
{"id":"tarleton-no2-seed-umhb-hosts-trinity-playoffs","seo":"Tarleton Gets No. 2 FCS Seed; UMHB Hosts Trinity Saturday","cat":"sports","city":"Central Texas","date":"2026-11-23","title":"Tarleton State earns No. 2 seed in the FCS playoffs; UMHB opens at home Saturday against Trinity","dek":"Unbeaten Tarleton gets a first-round bye and a home game Dec. 5 in Stephenville, while UMHB hosts Trinity in the NCAA Division III second round Nov. 28.","body":["Tarleton State is the No. 2 seed in the NCAA Division I FCS playoffs and will not play until Saturday, Dec. 5, when it hosts a second-round game in Stephenville, according to the bracket announced Sunday by the NCAA.","The Texans finished the regular season 12-0 and won the United Athletic Conference title outright. Their opponent will be the winner of a first-round game this weekend, and the game will stream on ESPN+. Kickoff time had not been announced. Read more: <a href=\"/news/tarleton-state-12-0-uac-title-north-alabama/\">Tarleton finishes 12-0</a>.","In Belton, Mary Hardin-Baylor (9-1) begins its Division III playoff run after a first-round bye. The Crusaders host Trinity at noon Saturday, Nov. 28, at Crusader Stadium, according to UMHB's schedule. The game streams on ESPN+.","Baylor (6-5) closes the regular season the same night at No. 17 Houston, 8:30 p.m. at TDECU Stadium on ESPN2, after a 20-10 home loss to Texas Tech.","Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],"sources":[["NCAA: 2026 FCS bracket and schedule","https://www.ncaa.com/news/football/article/2026-11-22/2026-fcs-football-championship-bracket-schedule-selection-info-playoffs","record"],["UMHB football schedule","https://cruathletics.com/sports/football/schedule/2026","record"],["Baylor Athletics: Baylor at Houston preview","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/11/22/football-baylor-heads-to-face-no-17-houston-on-saturday-night"]],"basis":"records"},
{"id":"wilsonart-temple-envases-waco-plant-filings","seo":"Wilsonart Temple, Envases Waco Plant Projects: $23.5M","cat":"growth","city":"Temple","date":"2026-11-23","basis":"records","top":1,"title":"State filings show a $13.5 million Wilsonart building in Temple and a $10 million Envases can plant expansion in Waco","dek":"Wilsonart's 124,800-square-foot Project Verne in Temple and a 140,000-square-foot Envases addition in Waco are both due to finish around Dec. 1.","body":["Two factory projects worth a combined $23.5 million are on track to wrap up in Temple and Waco around Dec. 1, according to state construction filings with the Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation.","<strong>Temple (Bell County):</strong> Wilsonart LLC registered a $13.5 million project called Project Verne at 10501 NW H.K. Dodgen Loop in north Temple's industrial area. The filing describes a new 124,800-square-foot pre-engineered metal building, with work scheduled from Feb. 1 to Dec. 1, 2026. The filing does not say what the building will be used for or how many people it will employ.","<strong>Waco (McLennan County):</strong> A filing titled Envases Can Plant Expansion lists a $10 million addition of about 140,000 square feet at 1901 Wycon Dr. The owner is listed as IZ Texas LLC, and the work was scheduled from June 1 to Dec. 1, 2026.","Neither company has announced hiring numbers tied to these projects, and we did not find local incentive agreements for either one. State filings record planned construction; dates often shift. Read more about Temple's industrial park: <a href=\"/news/temple-industrial-park-2026/\">where East Penn, Sesajal and SeAH stand</a>.","Track both projects: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/wilsonart-project-verne-temple/\">Wilsonart in Temple</a> and <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/envases-can-plant-expansion-waco/\">Envases in Waco</a>.","Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],"sources":[["TDLR filing TABS2026009620 (Project Verne, Temple)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Projects/TABS2026009620","record"],["TDLR filing TABS2026019758 (Envases Can Plant Expansion, Waco)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Projects/TABS2026019758","record"]]},
{"id":"nordstrom-rack-waco-central-texas-marketplace-filing","seo":"Nordstrom Rack Waco: $3M Store Filing at Texas Marketplace","cat":"business","also":["real-estate"],"city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-23","basis":"records","title":"Nordstrom Rack filing shows a $3 million store build-out at Central Texas Marketplace in Waco","dek":"A state filing lists a 28,847-square-foot Nordstrom Rack finish-out on South Jack Kultgen Expressway in Waco, with work set to end in March 2027.","body":["A $3 million interior build-out for a Nordstrom Rack store is registered at Central Texas Marketplace in Waco, according to a state construction filing with the Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation.","The filing describes a ground-floor tenant finish-out for a Nordstrom Rack department store in an existing one-story building at 4633 S. Jack Kultgen Expressway, Suite 106. It covers 28,847 square feet, with work scheduled from Oct. 16, 2026, to March 19, 2027. The property owner is listed as G3C Dodgen Multi-Outparcel LLC.","Nordstrom has not announced a Waco opening date, and we did not find a company announcement. Treat the store as planned, not confirmed to open, until the company says so.","More Waco openings and filings: <a href=\"/news/waco-business-roundup-nov-2026/\">Waco business roundup</a>.","See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],"sources":[["TDLR filing TABS2026018660 (Nordstrom Rack, Waco)","https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/TABS/Projects/TABS2026018660","record"]]},
{"id":"killeen-economic-development-policy-fast-track","seo":"Killeen's New Economic Development Policy: What Changes","cat":"growth","city":"Killeen","date":"2026-11-23","basis":"summary","title":"Killeen's proposed economic development policy adds fast-track reviews and help for north Killeen businesses","dek":"The plan up for a Killeen City Council vote adds 5-day permit checks, new state incentive tools and up to $20,000 for commercial sewer work.","body":["Short answer: Killeen's proposed economic development policy would speed up project reviews, add new state incentive tools and offer up to $20,000 to help north Killeen businesses with sewer work, if the City Council approves it in the coming weeks.","The Killeen Daily Herald laid out the draft after the council tabled it earlier this month. It would replace the city's current 10-point policy with a 12-step framework.","<strong>Fast track:</strong> the city would check applications for completeness within five days and aim to finish technical reviews in 10 to 20 business days.","<strong>New tools:</strong> the policy adds the state's JETI program, which can limit a project's school taxable value for 10 years, and the Texas Semiconductor Innovation Fund to the list of incentives Killeen can pursue.","<strong>North Killeen help:</strong> businesses could get a 50% match, up to $20,000, for commercial sewer improvements.","<strong>Other changes:</strong> the Innovation Black Chamber would be added as a workforce and AI training partner, and the council would review the policy every two years instead of every year.","No vote date had been set as of Monday. For who sits on the council, see <a href=\"/local-government/#killeen\">Who Runs the 254: Killeen</a>.","Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/business/a-look-at-killeen-s-proposed-new-economic-development-policy/article_c0e60ff1-a929-441d-bbae-0a535ee38dd2.html"]]},
{"id":"killeen-dec-3-closures-schools-city-offices","seo":"Killeen Closures Dec. 3: Schools, City Offices, Colleges","cat":"government","city":"Killeen","date":"2026-11-23","basis":"records","title":"What's closed in Killeen on Dec. 3: schools, city offices and two colleges","dek":"Killeen ISD, city offices, Central Texas College and Texas A&M-Central Texas plan Dec. 3 closures tied to the scheduled Nidal Hasan execution.","body":["Killeen ISD campuses, City of Killeen offices and the main campuses of Central Texas College and Texas A&M University-Central Texas will be closed Thursday, Dec. 3, according to the city and the schools.","The closures are tied to activity expected around the scheduled execution of Nidal Hasan, the former Army officer sentenced to death for the 2009 Fort Hood shooting.","<strong>City of Killeen:</strong> all city offices and facilities will be closed that day, according to a city news release. Thursday trash pickup moves to Wednesday, Dec. 2.","<strong>Killeen ISD:</strong> all campuses will be closed, the district announced Nov. 12.","<strong>Colleges:</strong> Central Texas College will close its main campus and move classes online, and Texas A&M-Central Texas will close its campus and hold classes online.","Check with each office or school for updates before Dec. 3. For Killeen's council and contacts, see <a href=\"/local-government/#killeen\">Who Runs the 254: Killeen</a>."],"sources":[["City of Killeen news release","https://www.killeentexas.gov/m/newsflash/Home/Detail/3152","record"],["KWTX: CTC main campus closing Dec. 3","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/16/ctc-main-campus-closing-dec-3-amid-expected-activity-surrounding-hasan-execution/"],["FOX 7 Austin: Killeen ISD districtwide closure","https://www.fox7austin.com/news/killeen-isd-districtwide-closure-nidal-hasan-execution-fort-hood-shooter"],["Texas A&M-Central Texas closure report","https://yahoo.com/news/us/articles/texas-m-central-texas-close-204822431.html"]]},
{"id":"temple-council-trail-contract-fire-station-12-land","seo":"Temple Council OKs $2.45M Trails, Fire Station 12 Land","cat":"government","city":"Temple","date":"2026-11-23","basis":"summary","title":"Temple council approves $2.45 million trail contract and land for a future Fire Station No. 12","dek":"Temple will build the Winding Oaks and West Temple Park trails and buy land on Lower Troy Road for a new fire station, while the old post office project grows to $6.29 million.","body":["The Temple City Council approved a $2.45 million contract to build two trails and agreed to buy land on Lower Troy Road for a future Fire Station No. 12, the Killeen Daily Herald reported.","<strong>Trails:</strong> Ratliff Hardscape Ltd. will build the Winding Oaks Trail and the West Temple Park Trail.","<strong>Fire Station No. 12:</strong> the city will buy property at 3659 Lower Troy Road for about $665,000 plus roughly $5,000 in closing costs. It is separate from the planned <a href=\"/news/temple-fire-station-9-old-waco-road/\">Fire Station 9 on Old Waco Road</a>.","<strong>Historic post office:</strong> a change order brings the downtown post office renovation to $6.29 million, about $3.75 million more than the original contract.","The council also approved an amendment with the Temple Economic Development Corp. covering 108.81 acres and sold a lot at 102 N. Pea Ridge Road to the Temple Revitalization Corp. for $1,000. Members also remembered Customer Care Director Heather Mikulas, who died after nearly 22 years with the city.","See the council roster: <a href=\"/local-government/#temple\">Who Runs the 254: Temple</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/temple-city-council-remembers-longtime-employee-approves-2-45-million-trail-project/article_1d935e00-4f38-54e0-934c-91b9b13aa56f.html"]]},
{"id":"gas-killeen-temple-3-dollars-thanksgiving-travel","seo":"Killeen-Temple Gas Hits $3.00 Before Thanksgiving Travel","cat":"markets","city":"Central Texas","date":"2026-11-23","basis":"summary","title":"Gas falls to about $3 in Killeen-Temple and Waco as 5.7 million Texans plan Thanksgiving trips","dek":"Regular gas averaged $3.00 in Killeen-Temple and $3.01 in Waco on Nov. 22, down 20 cents statewide in a week, per AAA.","body":["Regular gas averaged $3.00 a gallon in the Killeen-Temple-Fort Hood area and $3.01 in Waco on Sunday, Nov. 22, according to AAA, as prices kept sliding ahead of Thanksgiving.","The Texas average was $3.10, down from $3.30 a week earlier and $3.76 a month ago. That is still above last year's $2.68. Diesel averaged $5.05 in Killeen-Temple and $5.07 in Waco.","Drivers who shop around can do better. The Killeen Daily Herald reported the area's cheapest regular, per GasBuddy users, at $2.64 at Sam's Club in Harker Heights, and said local prices are down about 70 cents since Halloween.","<strong>Travel:</strong> AAA Texas expects about 5.7 million Texans to travel between Nov. 24 and Nov. 30, down 1.2% from last year, with 93% driving. INRIX says the worst days on the road are Tuesday and Wednesday before Thanksgiving and the Sunday and Monday after.","Earlier: <a href=\"/news/texas-gas-prices-thanksgiving-2026/\">why Texas is still headed for its priciest Thanksgiving at the pump since 2021</a>."],"sources":[["AAA Texas gas prices","https://gasprices.aaa.com/?state=TX","record"],["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/down-70-cents-since-halloween-gas-prices-keep-dropping-in-killeen-area/article_8526e8b3-913e-471a-80ca-b096907eba2f.html"],["FOX 4: Texas Thanksgiving travel forecast","https://www.fox4news.com/news/texas-thanksgiving-travel-forecast-worst-times-drive-2026"]]},
{"id":"belton-isd-legislative-priorities-2027","seo":"Belton ISD Sets Its Priorities for the 2027 Legislature","cat":"education","city":"Belton","date":"2026-11-23","basis":"summary","title":"Belton ISD board sets its priorities for the 2027 Legislature: funding, teacher pay and local control","dek":"After months of public input, Belton ISD trustees approved three legislative priorities: school funding, educator support including pay, and local control.","body":["The Belton ISD school board approved three priorities for the 2027 Texas Legislature at its Nov. 16 meeting: more state funding, support for educators including pay, and local control for districts, the Killeen Daily Herald reported.","The list came after months of public input, according to the report. Board President Chris Flor and Superintendent Malinda Golden spoke about the priorities, which the district will share with lawmakers before the session starts in January.","At the same meeting, state Rep. Brad Buckley presented resolutions honoring Lakewood Elementary and Lake Belton High School for earning A ratings from the Texas Education Agency.","Waco-area districts made a similar push this month. Read more: <a href=\"/news/waco-school-leaders-legislature-wish-list/\">What Waco, Midway and Connally ISD want from the Legislature</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen Daily Herald","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/belton-isd-board-approves-legislative-priorities-after-months-of-public-input/article_c556921a-b921-5cb1-bab0-798db6cd8a75.html"]]},
{"id":"waco-historic-church-2nd-and-clay-venue","seo":"Waco's Historic St. James Church Could Become Music Venue","cat":"business","city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-23","basis":"summary","title":"Waco couple plans to turn 102-year-old St. James church into a music and food venue called 2nd and Clay","dek":"Lane and Amy Murphy want to restore the historic Black church at Second Street and Clay Avenue in Waco as a place for food, music and a vinyl room.","body":["A Waco couple is working to save the 102-year-old St. James Methodist Church at Second Street and Clay Avenue and reopen it as a food and music venue called 2nd and Clay, KWTX reported.","Lane and Amy Murphy told KWTX they envision food, live music, a vinyl listening room and performance space in the historic Black church, and they are weighing a community ownership model.","The project will take a few million dollars, starting with a new roof, according to the report. No opening date has been set.","Track Waco openings: <a href=\"/news/waco-business-roundup-nov-2026/\">Waco business roundup</a>.","See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],"sources":[["KWTX","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/23/waco-couple-works-preserve-repurpose-102-year-old-historic-black-church/"]]},
{"id": "wine-basics-thanksgiving-wine", "cat": "things-to-do", "city": "Central Texas", "date": "2026-11-24", "author": "jake-ruse", "basis": "original", "title": "Wine Basics: What Wine Goes With Thanksgiving Dinner", "dek": "Skip the hunt for one perfect bottle. Light, high-acid reds, crisp whites and bubbles handle a Thanksgiving plate best.", "body": ["Short answer: pour a few light, high-acid wines, like bubbles, a crisp white and a soft red such as Pinot Noir, instead of hunting for one perfect bottle.", "Thanksgiving is the hardest plate of the year to pair. Turkey, cranberry sauce, green bean casserole, sweet potatoes with marshmallows and gravy all land at once, and no single wine is built for that. So stop hunting for the perfect bottle. Open three or four in different styles and let people pour whatever works with what's on their fork.", "The trait that matters most is acidity. It's what makes your mouth water, the same job lemon does on fried fish. Acid cuts through butter, gravy and salt and resets your palate between bites. A zesty Sauvignon Blanc handles the green bean casserole and the herbs in the dressing. Sparkling wine is the move for a fried turkey: bubbles plus acid scrub the fat right off your tongue.", "For red, go light and juicy, not big and dark. Pinot Noir, Beaujolais and Grenache bring tart red fruit that lines up with cranberry sauce and soft tannin that won't fight white meat. Cabernet Sauvignon, Syrah and Malbec are great wines, but their tannin and power steamroll turkey and clash with the sweet sides. Save the big Cab for steak night.", "Cooking method changes the call, so pair to the preparation, not just the bird. A smoked turkey, which plenty of 254 tables will have, can take more weight: Zinfandel or a Rhone-style blend of Grenache, Syrah and Mourvedre has the ripe fruit and spice to stand up to smoke. If the dressing has jalapeno or spicy sausage, pour a lower-alcohol Riesling with a touch of sweetness. Alcohol makes heat burn hotter, and a little sugar cools it down.", "Bubbles belong at the front door. They wake up everyone's palate, and nobody needs fancy flutes. Pie gets its own lane: a tawny Port or a late harvest Riesling stands up to pecan, pumpkin and caramel. The rule is simple: the wine has to be at least as sweet as the dessert, or the wine tastes sour.", "My advice: buy a few bottles in different styles, open them all and let people wander. Nobody at your table is grading you. The point is a full glass and a good conversation, not a perfect match.", "Takeaway: light, fresh and a few choices beats one big, expensive bottle.", "More from Jake: <a href=\"/sip-the-254/\">Sip the 254</a>."], "sources": [["Decanter: Thanksgiving wine pairings", "https://www.decanter.com/learn/thanksgiving-wine-pairings-and-15-american-wines-to-try-515609/"]]},
{"id":"waco-closures-jakes-tea-house-milk-bottle-nicolas-matthew","seo":"Waco Closings: Jake's Tea House, Milk Bottle, Baked Bliss","cat":"business","city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-24","basis":"summary","title":"Jake's Texas Tea House, Milk Bottle Cookies and Baked Bliss close in Waco as a new diner opens on Bosque","dek":"Three Waco small businesses are closing their storefronts this month, while chef-owned Nicolas Matthew diner opens at 5900 Bosque Blvd.","body":["Three small businesses in Waco, McLennan County, are closing or have closed their storefronts this month: Jake's Texas Tea House, Baked Bliss and the downtown Milk Bottle Cookies shop, Act Locally Waco reported Nov. 19.","<strong>Jake's Texas Tea House</strong> set Sunday, Nov. 22, as its last day, according to the report.","<strong>Baked Bliss</strong> is closing its storefront but was still taking Thanksgiving pie orders.","<strong>Milk Bottle Cookies</strong> is closing its downtown shop on South 11th Street. Owner Mackenzie Asisi said she wants more time with her family; the business started in her home kitchen in 2018.","<strong>New on Bosque:</strong> Nicolas Matthew, a diner from chef-owner James Quattrocchi, has opened at 5900 Bosque Blvd., the Baylor Lariat reported Nov. 18. Quattrocchi named it for his two sons, and the menu runs from rock cakes, croissants, donuts and muffins to pies, lasagna and sandwiches.","More Waco openings: <a href=\"/news/waco-business-roundup-nov-2026/\">Waco business roundup</a>.","See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],"sources":[["Act Locally Waco: Waco small business closures","https://actlocallywaco.org/2026/11/19/waco-small-business-closures/"],["Baylor Lariat: New diner gives customers taste of home","https://baylorlariat.com/2026/11/18/new-diner-gives-customers-taste-of-home/"]]},
{"id":"temple-edc-land-11-acres-fm-3117","seo":"Temple Adds 11.7 Acres to EDC Land Near FM 3117","cat":"growth","city":"Temple","date":"2026-11-24","basis":"summary","title":"Temple adds 11.7 acres near FM 3117 to land held by its economic development corporation","dek":"The Temple City Council grew the land the Temple EDC holds for future commercial use between Lorraine Avenue and FM 3117 to 108.81 acres.","body":["The Temple City Council has added about 11.7 acres between Lorraine Avenue and FM 3117 to the land the Temple Economic Development Corp. holds for future commercial use, the Temple Daily Telegram reported Nov. 21 in a story shared by the Killeen Daily Herald.","The vote amended the city's land agreement with the EDC. The four connected properties in Temple, Bell County, now total 108.81 acres, with a combined appraised value of $443,396 and a city cost basis of $17,579.29, according to the report.","<strong>Taxes:</strong> the land stays tax-exempt while the EDC holds it and goes back on the tax rolls once it is conveyed for a commercial use. The report did not name a project for the site.","<strong>Also at the meeting:</strong> a $59,726 change order for the Historic Post Office renovation brings that project to about $6.29 million, roughly $3.75 million more than the original $2.54 million contract. The council also approved a $2.45 million trail contract and land for a future fire station (<a href=\"/news/temple-council-trail-contract-fire-station-12-land/\">our earlier story</a>).","Where Temple's big industrial projects stand: <a href=\"/news/temple-industrial-park-2026/\">East Penn, Sesajal and SeAH</a>.","Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen Daily Herald / Temple Daily Telegram","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/temple-city-council-remembers-longtime-employee-approves-2-45-million-trail-project/article_1d935e00-4f38-54e0-934c-91b9b13aa56f.html"]]},
{"id":"killeen-water-wastewater-impact-fees-dec-8-vote","seo":"Killeen Impact Fees Could Triple: Dec. 8 Council Vote","cat":"growth","also":["real-estate"],"city":"Killeen","date":"2026-11-24","basis":"summary","title":"Killeen weighs nearly tripling water and sewer impact fees on new homes: what to know before the Dec. 8 vote","dek":"Killeen's proposed impact fees would take the one-time charge on a typical new home from $1,579 to $4,745. The council votes Dec. 8.","body":["Short answer: Killeen's proposed water and wastewater impact fees would raise the one-time charge for a typical new home connection in Killeen, Bell County, from $1,579 to $4,745, about 200% more, and the City Council is scheduled to take the plan back up on Dec. 8.","<strong>The numbers:</strong> per service unit (a standard 3/4-inch meter), the water fee would go from $1,161 to $3,764 and the wastewater fee from $418 to $1,080, the Killeen Daily Herald reported. An engineering study put the most the city could charge at $4,844.","<strong>Why it was tabled:</strong> on Nov. 17 the council voted unanimously to hold off, citing unclear ordinance wording, worries that developers would pass the cost to home buyers, and the fact that staff had not yet met with builders. \"Details do matter,\" Councilwoman Mellisa Brown said. The city attorney said the council must act within 30 days, which is why it returns Dec. 8.","<strong>What's at stake:</strong> charging the maximum could bring in about $4.7 million a year, compared with about $1.39 million budgeted for fiscal 2027, according to a Nov. 22 Herald analysis. Impact fees are paid on new development and help cover water and sewer lines and plants.","<strong>Building is up:</strong> Killeen issued 549 single-family permits from January through October 2026, about 30% more than the 422 in the same stretch a year earlier, the Herald reported.","Earlier: <a href=\"/news/bell-county-councils-roundup-nov-20/\">Bell County council roundup</a>. How to reach the council: <a href=\"/local-government/#killeen\">Who Runs the 254: Killeen</a>.","Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen Daily Herald: Council tables water impact fees","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/killeen-council-tables-water-impact-fees-after-concerns-over-details-and-stakeholder-input/article_475a0a0f-53e0-4dd1-bec9-b9abe89d684e.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: The price of growth","https://kdhnews.com/business/the-price-of-growth-is-killeen-becoming-too-expensive-for-its-own-residents/article_79ed595f-bc5a-4c34-aa5e-d891162b35b1.html"]]},
{"id":"bell-county-treasurer-elect-hodges-lawsuit-salary","seo":"Bell County Treasurer-Elect Sues Over Withheld Salary","cat":"government","city":"Bell County","date":"2026-11-24","basis":"summary","title":"Bell County treasurer-elect sues over the state law used to cut her salary","dek":"Adriane Hodges says the law that let Bell County commissioners zero out the treasurer's $115,028 salary violates the First Amendment.","body":["Bell County Treasurer-elect Adriane Hodges has filed a federal First Amendment lawsuit challenging the state law Bell County commissioners used to eliminate the treasurer's $115,028 salary starting Jan. 1, 2027, the Temple Daily Telegram reported Nov. 21.","Hodges is represented by the Foundation for Individual Rights and Expression (FIRE). The suit targets Texas Local Government Code 152.052, which lets a county withhold pay from an official who campaigned on abolishing their own office. Hodges campaigned on moving the treasurer's duties to the county auditor, and commissioners voted unanimously to eliminate the salary.","<strong>The claims:</strong> the suit argues the law discriminates based on viewpoint and that a required affidavit, saying she voluntarily declined the salary, is compelled speech. \"I don't think that I should be compelled to lie,\" Hodges said.","<strong>The county:</strong> County Judge David Blackburn said he was unaware of the suit, according to the report. Commissioners met in closed session Monday to appoint legal counsel and did not say what it was for.","<strong>Background:</strong> earlier this month FIRE filed a separate federal case in Waco against the Texas Ethics Commission so it could represent Hodges for free. That complaint said FIRE planned a separate challenge to the salary law against Bell County.","Who serves on the court and how to reach it: <a href=\"/local-government/#bell-county\">Who Runs the 254: Bell County</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen Daily Herald / Temple Daily Telegram","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/bell-county-treasurer-elect-files-first-amendment-lawsuit-against-state-law-commissioners-court/article_2b3fb688-9fa3-56bd-a1c0-6500972a36f2.html"],["FIRE v. Texas Ethics Commission complaint, W.D. Tex. No. 6:26-cv-00699","https://texasscorecard.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Complaint-AS-FILED.pdf","record"]]},
{"id":"dec-12-runoffs-copperas-cove-bell-county-appraisal","seo":"Dec. 12 Runoffs in Copperas Cove and Bell County","cat":"government","city":"Copperas Cove","date":"2026-11-24","basis":"summary","title":"Dec. 12 runoffs: Copperas Cove council Place 6 and a Bell County appraisal board seat are on the ballot","dek":"Copperas Cove picks a Place 6 council member and Bell County an appraisal board member in Dec. 12 runoffs. Here's who is on the ballot.","body":["Runoff elections on Saturday, Dec. 12, 2026, will settle a Copperas Cove City Council seat and a seat on the Bell County Appraisal District board.","<strong>Copperas Cove, Place 6:</strong> Jesus Mendez (3,447 votes on Nov. 3) faces Jay Manning (3,207), the Killeen Daily Herald reported. The city posted its official runoff notice Nov. 20. The notice also lists Place 7, but that runoff is off after a candidate withdrew (<a href=\"/news/copperas-cove-place-7-runoff-withdrawal/\">our story</a>). Questions go to City Secretary Lisa Wilson at (254) 547-4221 or Coryell County Voter Registrar Justin Carothers at (254) 865-5911.","<strong>Bell County Appraisal District, Place 2:</strong> James Butts (30,788 votes, 41.8%) faces Gwendolyn Everett (26,839 votes, 36.44%). Early voting in Bell County runs Nov. 30 through Dec. 8, and the runoff is expected to cost about $210,696, according to Elections Administrator Desi Roberts. What the board does: <a href=\"/news/we-the-people-bellcad-runoff/\">our explainer</a>.","Council members, meeting times and contacts: <a href=\"/local-government/#copperas-cove\">Who Runs the 254: Copperas Cove</a>."],"sources":[["City of Copperas Cove: Notice of runoff election","https://www.copperascovetx.gov/m/newsflash/Home/Detail/156","record"],["Notice of Runoff Election (PDF)","https://www.copperascovetx.gov/DocumentCenter/View/7303/Notice-of-Runoff-Election-2026-PDF","record"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Cove canvass","https://kdhnews.com/copperas_cove_herald/cove-council-vote-canvass-set-runoff-elections-to-come/article_a9841607-3cfc-42bb-80d8-d8f6fa024873.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Appraisal district runoff cost","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/bell-county-appraisal-district-runoff-to-cost-210-696-amid-billing-delays/article_51b04693-1e18-505e-9dd0-f52e07ff4bdc.html"],["Bell CAD board elections","https://bellcad.org/board-of-directors-elections/","record"]]},
{"id":"copperas-cove-isd-new-trustees-board-officers","seo":"Copperas Cove ISD Swears In Three New Trustees","cat":"education","city":"Copperas Cove","date":"2026-11-24","basis":"summary","title":"Copperas Cove ISD swears in three trustees; board picks officers on 4-3 votes","dek":"James Ortiz, Trang Nguyen and returning trustee Jeff Gorres took the oath, and Tim Traeger was named Copperas Cove ISD board president.","body":["Copperas Cove ISD swore in three school board members at a special meeting last week and chose new board officers, two of them on split votes, the Copperas Cove Herald reported Nov. 20.","<strong>Sworn in:</strong> James Ortiz, Place 5, who won with 56.1% of the vote; Trang Nguyen, Place 6, with 57%; and incumbent Jeff Gorres, Place 7, with 53.1%.","<strong>Officers:</strong> Tim Traeger was elected president unanimously. Joan Manning was chosen vice president and Sherry Hoffpauir secretary, each on a 4-3 vote, with Gorres, Nguyen and Traeger voting no.","The district's online board list had not been updated with the new members as of Nov. 24."],"sources":[["Copperas Cove Herald (KDH)","https://kdhnews.com/copperas_cove_herald/newly-elected-copperas-cove-school-trustees-take-oath-of-office-board-officers-appointed/article_4eb31276-5648-44b9-9f9d-6fc5fb4fa8fe.html"],["Copperas Cove ISD board members","https://ccisd.com/page/board-members"]]},
{"id":"baylor-time-best-colleges-future-leaders-2027","seo":"Baylor No. 82 on TIME Best Colleges for Future Leaders","cat":"education","city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-24","basis":"records","title":"Baylor ranks No. 82 on TIME's Best Colleges for Future Leaders list","dek":"Baylor University in Waco made TIME's 2027 list for a fourth straight year, ranking fifth in Texas and sixth in the Big 12.","body":["Baylor University in Waco ranked No. 82 nationally on TIME's Best Colleges for Future Leaders 2027 list, the university announced Nov. 19. Baylor placed fifth among Texas schools and sixth in the Big 12, its fourth straight year on the list.","TIME and the research firm Statista built the ranking from a survey of about 5,900 leaders, according to Baylor. The magazine singled out Baylor's Hankamer School of Business.","\"Leadership development is woven throughout the Baylor educational experience,\" President Linda A. Livingstone said.","<strong>Also this week:</strong> Baylor faculty took their research into McLennan County classrooms for National STEM Day, the university said, teaching magnetism at Midway ISD's Park Hill Elementary, DNA copying and repair at Lorena Middle School and pollination tool design at La Vega High School. It was the seventh year for the program."],"sources":[["Baylor University news release","https://news.web.baylor.edu/news/story/2026/baylor-university-named-times-best-colleges-future-leaders-2027-list","record"],["Baylor University: National STEM Day","https://news.web.baylor.edu/news/story/2026/baylor-faculty-celebrate-national-stem-day-bringing-research-local-classrooms","record"]]},
{"id":"killeen-temple-waco-unemployment-october-2026","seo":"Killeen-Temple, Waco Unemployment Rises in October","cat":"markets","city":"Central Texas","date":"2026-11-24","basis":"records","title":"Unemployment ticks up to 5.0% in Killeen-Temple and 4.2% in Waco as Texas adds 30,600 jobs","dek":"The Texas Workforce Commission's October report shows Killeen-Temple and Waco jobless rates edging up even as Texas added 30,600 jobs.","body":["The unemployment rate rose to 5.0% in the Killeen-Temple metro (Bell, Coryell and Lampasas counties) and 4.2% in the Waco metro in October, the Texas Workforce Commission reported Nov. 20, while Texas added 30,600 jobs for the month.","<strong>Local trend:</strong> Killeen-Temple was up from 4.9% in September and Waco from 4.0%. Both are still below August, when Killeen-Temple stood at 5.2% and Waco at 4.3%, according to TWC. The metro rates are not seasonally adjusted, so they move with the calendar.","<strong>Statewide:</strong> Texas has added 203,300 jobs over the past year, a 1.4% gain, and the seasonally adjusted state rate held at 4.4%. Professional and business services led October with 13,600 new jobs, followed by construction with 6,900 and trade, transportation and utilities with 6,100.","<strong>How we compare:</strong> Midland had the state's lowest metro rate at 3.2% and Eagle Pass the highest at 6.4%."],"sources":[["Texas Workforce Commission: October jobs report","https://www.twc.texas.gov/news/texas-gains-more-30000-nonfarm-jobs-october","record"],["Texas Workforce Commission: August report","https://www.twc.texas.gov/news/annual-job-growth-exceeds-159000-texas","record"]]},
{"id":"baylor-week-alabama-las-vegas-wbb-volleyball-houston","seo":"Baylor Basketball vs. Alabama in Las Vegas: Week Ahead","cat":"sports","city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-24","basis":"summary","top":1,"title":"Baylor's big week: men face No. 15 Alabama in Las Vegas, women rout Northern Kentucky, football closes at Houston","dek":"Baylor men's basketball (4-1) opens the Players Era event tonight in Las Vegas, and Baylor women, volleyball and football all play this week.","body":["Baylor men's basketball (4-1) plays No. 15 Alabama (5-0) at 9 p.m. Central on Tuesday, Nov. 24, at T-Mobile Arena in Las Vegas in the first round of the Players Era event, on ESPN2, Baylor Athletics said.","<strong>Men:</strong> a win sends the Bears to a Thursday semifinal against the Gonzaga-Kansas State winner, with placement games Nov. 27 and the title game Nov. 28. Baylor's last outing was a 104-55 rout of Jackson State on Nov. 18, when Brett Decker Jr. scored a career-high 35 and tied the school record with 10 three-pointers. The only loss is 75-72 to No. 7 Texas.","<strong>Women:</strong> Baylor fell 78-69 to No. 4 USC on Nov. 20 despite a season-high 24 points from Taliah Scott, the Baylor Lariat reported, then beat Northern Kentucky 96-42 at Foster Pavilion on Nov. 22. Next up is Penn State on Friday at the Paradise Jam.","<strong>Volleyball:</strong> No. 20 Baylor beat Iowa State in five sets Nov. 20, then took the first two sets against No. 8 Arizona State on senior day Nov. 22 before losing in five. The Bears close the regular season on the road this week, and the NCAA tournament field is revealed Sunday, Nov. 29.","<strong>Football:</strong> Baylor (6-5, 4-4 Big 12) is bowl-eligible and closes the regular season at No. 17 Houston at 8:30 p.m. Saturday on ESPN2. The Bears are 2-2 under interim coach Joe Klanderman after the 20-10 loss to Texas Tech (<a href=\"/news/baylor-falls-texas-tech-20-10-senior-day/\">our story</a>).","Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],"sources":[["Baylor Athletics: MBB vs. Alabama preview","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/11/23/mens-basketball-mbb-takes-on-no-15-15-alabama-at-players-era-16","record"],["Baylor Lariat: Baylor falls to No. 4 USC","https://baylorlariat.com/2026/11/21/baylors-upset-bid-fails-against-no-4-usc-despite-hot-start/"],["Baylor Athletics: WBB beats Northern Kentucky","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/11/22/womens-basketball-wbb-overpowers-northern-kentucky-in-96-42-victory","record"],["Baylor Lariat: Volleyball beats Iowa State","https://baylorlariat.com/2026/11/21/no-20-baylor-volleyball-sneaks-past-iowa-state-in-gutsy-5-set-win/"],["Baylor Athletics: Volleyball vs. Arizona State","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/11/22/volleyball-no-20-vb-pushes-no-8-arizona-state-to-five-sets-on-senior-day","record"],["Baylor Athletics: Football at Houston","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/11/22/football-baylor-heads-to-face-no-17-houston-on-saturday-night","record"]]},
{"id": "golf-which-tees-should-i-play", "cat": "sports", "city": "Central Texas", "date": "2026-11-24", "golf": "basics", "basis": "original", "title": "Golf Basics: Which Tees Should I Play?", "dek": "Pick your tees by how far you hit your driver or 7-iron, not by habit. Here is the USGA and PGA of America chart and how to use it on 254 courses.", "body": ["Short answer: play the tees whose total length matches how far you hit your driver, which for most new golfers means moving up.", "Most courses have several sets of tee markers on every hole. Each set makes the course a different length. The back tees can be over 7,000 yards. The forward tees can be under 5,000. Same holes, very different day.", "In 2011 the PGA of America and the USGA launched Tee It Forward to get golfers to match course length to their game. Their guideline chart starts with your average driver distance:", "<ul><li>275 yards: 6,700 to 6,900 yards</li><li>250 yards: 6,200 to 6,400 yards</li><li>225 yards: 5,800 to 6,000 yards</li><li>200 yards: 5,200 to 5,400 yards</li><li>175 yards: 4,400 to 4,600 yards</li><li>150 yards: 3,500 to 3,700 yards</li></ul>", "Use your real average, not your best one. Driver distance varies a lot by swing speed, so if you don't know yours, hit a bucket at the range and note where most balls finish. Then look at the total yardage for each tee on the scorecard and pick the set inside your range.", "The USGA's newer \"Best Tees\" approach uses the 7-iron instead, because most golfers know that number better. The Texas Golf Association, writing about that research, puts the average 7-iron at about 138 yards for men and 100 yards for women. On a standard par-72 layout, that points the average man to about 6,100 yards and the average woman to about 4,400.", "Here is the simple test from that research. A tee fits when you can comfortably reach the fairway on par 4s and par 5s, get near most greens in regulation, and hit a mix of clubs into greens. If you are hitting a fairway wood into every par 4, you are too far back.", "Most golfers are. The TGA article says more than 80% of golfers in the USGA's survey were playing tees too long for them.", "Moving up does not hurt your handicap. Every set of tees has its own Course Rating and Slope Rating, and the World Handicap System adjusts your Course Handicap for the tees you play. Friends can play different tees and still have a fair match.", "Course length is not the whole story. The USGA notes that forced carries, deep bunkers and raised greens make some courses play harder than the scorecard says. On a tough or hilly course, move up one more set.", "That matters around here. Bear Ridge in Waco stretches to 7,478 yards from the tips but offers six sets of tees. Cottonwood Creek, Waco's city course, plays more than 7,200 from the back and also has a nine-hole par-3 course for brand-new players. Hancock Park in Lampasas is about 6,000 yards from the back, which suits a lot of golfers as-is.", "The payoff: shorter irons into greens, fewer lost balls and faster rounds. Pick the tees your game fits, not the ones your buddies play.", "More: <a href=\"/golf/\">Golf in the 254</a>."], "sources": [["USGA: Tee It Forward to increase enjoyment of the game", "https://www.usga.org/articles/2011/05/tee-it-forward-to-increase-enjoyment-of-the-game-2147497765.html", "record"], ["Tee It Forward guidelines chart (PGA of America/USGA, via MassGolf)", "https://www.massgolf.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/Tee_It_Forward_Guidelines.pdf"], ["Texas Golf Association: Choosing the right tees", "https://read.nxtbook.com/texas_golf_association/lone_star_golf/february_2026/choosing_the_right_tees.html"], ["USGA: Playing a match from different tees", "https://www.usga.org/content/usga/home-page/members/world-handicap-system-playing-a-golf-match-from-different-tees.html", "record"]]},
{id:"hike-pick-first-trail", cat:"things-to-do", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-24", trail:"basics", basis:"original",
 title:"Hiking 101: How do I pick my first trail?",
 dek:"How to pick your first hiking trail in Central Texas: start short, flat and well marked, with four easy first picks in the 254.",
 body:[
  "Short answer: pick a trail that is short, mostly flat and clearly marked. The Appalachian Mountain Club says to start with hikes of about 2 to 3 miles round trip with little or very gentle elevation gain. Build up from there.",
  "<strong>Be honest about your shape:</strong> REI's first advice on choosing a hike is to honestly assess what kind of shape you're in. The American Hiking Society says a relatively short trail with lower total elevation gain is ideal, and to stick with well-maintained, clearly marked trails until you feel comfortable navigating.",
  "<strong>Read two numbers:</strong> distance and elevation gain. REI says a trail that gains 1,000 feet in one mile is quite steep. Our trail list rates every trail Easy, Moderate or Hard and notes the surface and shade. For a first hike, stick with Easy.",
  "<strong>Four easy first picks in the 254:</strong> The Andy K. Wells Hike and Bike Trail in Killeen is a paved 2.5-mile path with restrooms along the way. The Pepper Creek Hike & Bike Trail in Temple is paved and about 5.6 miles long, so walk out and turn back when you hit your distance. The Waco Lake Dam Hike & Bike Trail is paved and about 2 miles one way, with wide lake views and almost no shade. Mother Neff State Park near Moody has the 0.6-mile Prairie Loop, an easy dirt trail that works for kids. A daily state park entry fee applies there.",
  "<strong>Plan your time:</strong> REI says an average walking pace is about 3 mph, but your hiking pace may be slower depending on terrain and elevation gain. Its rule of thumb is to add an hour for every 1,000 feet of elevation gain. Plan on more time on dirt and rock than on pavement.",
  "<strong>Watch the clock this time of year:</strong> REI says that in fall, when the sun sets earlier, you should plan so you're not caught out after dark. Check sunset before you start.",
  "<strong>Tell someone:</strong> REI says to always leave a detailed itinerary with a friend or family member. The American Hiking Society says to let people know where you're hiking and when you plan to be back.",
  "<strong>Turning around is fine:</strong> the American Hiking Society says you can always turn around if a trail feels too challenging. The AMC says don't hesitate to turn back if the weather takes a turn for the worse.",
  "<strong>Make sure it's open:</strong> the American Hiking Society says to confirm the trail and trailhead are open before you go. Right now, Texas Parks and Wildlife says the south gate at Mother Neff is closed. Dana Peak Park in Harker Heights is closed October through March. The City of Waco has closed part of the Riverwalk, from Jackson Avenue to the Baylor Law School, for construction expected to run through January 2028.",
  "More: <a href=\"/trails/\">Trails & Hiking in the 254</a>."],
 sources:[["REI Expert Advice: Hiking for Beginners","https://www.rei.com/learn/expert-advice/hiking-for-beginners"],["American Hiking Society: Hiking for Beginners","https://americanhiking.org/hiking-for-beginners-essential-guide/"],["Appalachian Mountain Club: Avoid these common beginner hiking mistakes","https://www.outdoors.org/resources/amc-outdoors/outdoor-resources/avoid-these-common-beginner-hiking-mistakes/"],["Texas Parks and Wildlife: Mother Neff State Park alerts","https://tpwd.texas.gov/state-parks/mother-neff/alert","record"]]},
{id:"bellcad-runoff-gwendolyn-everett-james-butts", seo:"Gwendolyn Everett vs. James Butts: BellCAD Runoff Dec. 12", cat:"government", city:"Belton", date:"2026-11-24", basis:"records",
 title:"Bell County Appraisal District runoff: Gwendolyn Everett vs. James Butts, what to know before Dec. 12",
 dek:"James Butts and Gwendolyn Everett face off Dec. 12 for Place 2 on the Bell County Appraisal District board: the results, key dates and what the seat does.",
 body:[
  "Short answer: James Butts and Gwendolyn Everett meet in a Saturday, Dec. 12, runoff for Place 2 on the Bell County Appraisal District board of directors, and early voting in Bell County runs Nov. 30 through Dec. 8.",
  "<strong>How they got here.</strong> Three candidates ran for Place 2 on Nov. 3: James Butts, Paul Strang and Gwendolyn Everett, according to the appraisal district's election page. Butts led with 30,788 votes (41.8%) and Everett finished second with 26,839 votes (36.44%), the Killeen Daily Herald reported. No one topped 50%, so the top two go to a runoff. The race is nonpartisan.",
  "<strong>What the seat does.</strong> The appraisal district, known as BellCAD, sets the value of every taxable property in Bell County. Its board hires the chief appraiser, approves the district's budget and contracts, and sets general policy, according to BellCAD. The board does not appraise property, hear protests or change appraisal records. Tax rates are set by your city, county and school district, not BellCAD. Our explainer has more: <a href=\"/news/we-the-people-bellcad-runoff/\">what the BellCAD board does</a>.",
  "<strong>About the candidates.</strong> Neither candidate had posted a biography or platform on the public candidate profile pages we checked as of Nov. 24, and BellCAD's election page lists names only. We will add background on both candidates when it is published on the record. Candidates can reach us through our <a href=\"/contact/\">contact page</a>.",
  "<strong>Key dates.</strong> The deadline to register for this runoff was Nov. 12. Applications for a mail ballot must be received by Tuesday, Dec. 1. Early voting runs Monday, Nov. 30, through Tuesday, Dec. 8, according to the Texas Secretary of State's runoff calendar. Election Day is Saturday, Dec. 12.",
  "<strong>Where to vote.</strong> Expect fewer polling places than in November. The county will use 21 Election Day sites instead of 42 to cut the cost of the runoff, which BellCAD reimburses. Check the Bell County Elections Office for early voting and Election Day locations before you go.",
  "The same day, Copperas Cove voters settle a City Council runoff. Both races: <a href=\"/news/dec-12-runoffs-copperas-cove-bell-county-appraisal/\">Dec. 12 runoffs in the 254</a>. Who represents you: <a href=\"/local-government/\">Who Runs the 254</a>."],
 sources:[["Bell CAD: Board of Directors elections","https://bellcad.org/board-of-directors-elections/","record"],["Texas Secretary of State: Dec. 12, 2026 runoff election calendar","https://www.sos.state.tx.us/elections/laws/advisory2026-27-dec-12-runoff-election-law-calendar.shtml","record"],["Bell County Elections Office: notices","https://www.bellcountytx.com/departments/elections/Notices.php","record"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Appraisal district runoff","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/bell-county-appraisal-district-runoff-to-cost-210-696-amid-billing-delays/article_51b04693-1e18-505e-9dd0-f52e07ff4bdc.html"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Bell County canvass","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/bell-county-canvasses-november-election-accepts-16-75-million-in-grants/article_fab21c7d-5c44-530b-8b28-c8067084627a.html"]]},
{id:"thanksgiving-2026-trash-pickup-closures-254", seo:"Thanksgiving Trash Pickup & Closures: Temple, Killeen, Waco", cat:"government", city:"Central Texas", date:"2026-11-24", basis:"records",
 title:"Thanksgiving 2026 in the 254: trash pickup changes, city closures and what's open",
 dek:"Killeen runs Thursday trash a day early while Temple, Harker Heights and Waco run it a day late. Here's what's closed and open Nov. 26 and 27.",
 body:[
  "Short answer: most 254 cities skip trash pickup on Thanksgiving, Thursday, Nov. 26, but Killeen moves its Thursday routes a day early to Wednesday, Nov. 25, while Temple, Harker Heights, Copperas Cove and Waco push them to Friday, Nov. 27.",
  "<strong>Temple:</strong> no trash or recycling pickup Thursday and the landfill is closed. Thursday routes run Friday and Friday routes run Saturday, according to the city's solid waste page.",
  "<strong>Killeen:</strong> Thursday routes run Wednesday, Nov. 25. City offices, libraries, the Transfer Station and the Recycling Center are closed Thursday and Friday, and offices reopen Monday, Nov. 30, according to the city.",
  "<strong>Harker Heights:</strong> trash runs a day late, with Thursday routes on Friday and Friday routes on Saturday. City Hall and the library are closed Thursday through Sunday, according to the city's Thanksgiving notice.",
  "<strong>Copperas Cove:</strong> no pickup Thursday. Areas 7 and 8 move to Friday, and all city facilities are closed Thursday and Friday, according to the city's holiday schedule.",
  "<strong>Waco:</strong> Thursday carts are picked up Friday. City offices are closed Thursday and Friday, libraries close at 6 p.m. Wednesday through Friday, and Waco Transit doesn't run Thursday, according to the city.",
  "<strong>Belton:</strong> the city's standing rule is that trash runs a day late the rest of the week after a weekday holiday. Belton had not posted a 2026 notice as of Tuesday.",
  "<strong>Everyone:</strong> post offices are closed Thursday with no regular mail delivery, and Thursday is a Federal Reserve holiday, so most banks are closed. The HOP runs no buses Thursday; on Friday only the Cavazos Connector runs, 11 a.m. to 10 p.m. H-E-B is open 6 a.m. to noon Thursday with the pharmacy closed, while Walmart, Target and Costco are closed.",
  "Every schedule, with links to each official source, is on our <a href=\"/holiday-hours/\">Holiday Hours in the 254</a> page. Need a free meal? See <a href=\"/food-help/\">Free Meals & Food Help</a>."],
 sources:[["City of Temple: Solid Waste Services","https://www.templetx.gov/departments/city_departments/public_works/garbage___recycling/index.php","record"],["City of Killeen: holiday closures","https://www.killeentexas.gov/Calendar.aspx?EID=5320","record"],["City of Harker Heights: Thanksgiving 2026 hours","https://www.harkerheights.gov/m/newsflash/Home/Detail/35","record"],["City of Copperas Cove: Thanksgiving schedule (PDF)","https://www.copperascovetx.gov/DocumentCenter/View/7281/City-Holiday-Schedule---Thanksgiving-PDF","record"],["City of Waco: Thanksgiving closures","https://www.waco-texas.com/News/Holiday-Closures/Thanksgiving","record"],["USPS newsroom","https://about.usps.com/newsroom/national-releases/2026/1117-usps-to-close-for-thanksgiving-holiday-on-nov-26.htm","record"],["The HOP: holiday service","https://takethehop.com/service-holiday-schedule","record"],["H-E-B: holiday hours","https://newsroom.heb.com/holiday-hours-at-heb/"]]},
{"id": "wine-basics-how-long-open-wine-lasts", "cat": "things-to-do", "city": "Central Texas", "date": "2026-11-25", "author": "jake-ruse", "basis": "original", "title": "Wine Basics: How Long Does an Open Bottle Last?", "dek": "Most open reds and whites last three to five days with the cork back in, bubbly about one to three. Cold is what buys you time.", "body": ["Short answer: most open wine holds up three to five days with the cork or cap back on and the bottle kept cold, and bubbly lasts one to three.", "After tomorrow's dinner, plenty of half-finished bottles will be sitting on kitchen counters across the 254. The clock starts the moment the cork comes out. Oxygen gets in and slowly flattens the fruit, and given time, acetic acid bacteria turn the alcohol into acetic acid, the sour stuff in vinegar. Both reactions slow way down in the cold. That's the whole reason the fridge works.", "Here's the rough clock, closure back on and bottle in the fridge. Sparkling wine: one to three days with a proper sparkling stopper. Light, crisp whites and rosé: three to five days, sometimes longer. Fuller whites like oaked Chardonnay or Viognier: about three, because they fade faster. Reds: three to five. Port and other fortified wines: a few weeks, since the extra alcohol protects them. If you're picky, trust the short end.", "Yes, put the red in the fridge too. A 70-degree kitchen wears out an open bottle fast. Pull it out 20 to 30 minutes before you pour so it isn't ice cold. Reds with more tannin and acid hold on longest, and a young, tight red can actually taste better on day two.", "Skip the folklore. A spoon in the neck of a Champagne bottle does nothing for the bubbles. A vacuum pump buys a day or two at best. Boxed wine is the long-haul champ: the bag collapses as you pour, so air barely touches what's left, and it holds two to three weeks in the fridge after opening. Don't push it past a month.", "How do you know it's done? Smell it. Sharp vinegar or nail polish, or a flat, nutty, bruised-apple taste, means it's gone. A white turning golden brown or a red going brick orange is the same story. A bottle that's only a little dull still works great in a pan sauce or a pot of chili.", "The takeaway: cork it, chill it and finish it by the weekend.", "More from Jake: <a href=\"/sip-the-254/\">Sip the 254</a>."], "sources": [["Decanter: How long does wine last after opening?", "https://www.decanter.com/learn/advice/putting-wine-fridge-ask-decanter-296127/"]]},
{"id": "golf-wedge-clock-system", "cat": "sports", "city": "Central Texas", "date": "2026-11-25", "golf": "advanced", "basis": "original", "title": "Lower Your Score: Dial In Your Wedges With the Clock System", "dek": "The wedge clock system turns each wedge into three or four shots by using backswing length to control distance inside 100 yards.", "body": ["Short answer: Keep the same tempo and change only how far you swing back. A shorter backswing hits the ball shorter. Learn three lengths and every wedge in your bag gives you three more distances.", "Why it matters. Most scores leak inside 100 yards. A full swing is easy to repeat. The in-between shots are not. If you try to guess a three-quarter swing, you will decelerate, chunk it or fly the green. The clock gives you a fixed picture instead of a feel.", "How it works. Picture yourself standing in the middle of a clock face, with the ball at 6 o'clock. Your lead arm is the hour hand. GOLF.com lays out three backswing stops: 7:30, 9:00 and 10:30. Per that article, 7:30 goes about half your full distance, 9:00 about 75 percent and 10:30 about 90 percent.", "Run the math. Say your gap wedge flies 100 yards with a full swing. The clock gives you roughly 50, 75 and 90 from that one club. Do the same with your pitching wedge and sand wedge and you have a dozen numbers to pick from. Your numbers will be different. They vary by swing speed, strike and the wedge's loft, so you have to measure your own.", "Keep the rhythm the same. This is the part people skip. The system only works if the tempo stays constant and the backswing length is the only thing that changes. GOLF.com stresses a consistent rhythm. Golf Magic's version of the drill, from coach Gary Boyd, adds a key point: accelerate through the ball. Do not slow down into impact.", "How to build your chart. Rehearse each position without a club first, as Boyd suggests. Then go to the range or a practice area with yardage flags. Hit five balls with one wedge at 7:30. Note where they land, not where they roll. Repeat at 9:00 and 10:30. Do this for each wedge. Write the carry numbers on a small card or in your phone and bring it to the course.", "Central Texas notes. Measure carry, not total. Our summer fairways and greens run firm, so the ball releases more in August than it will in a damp January. Wind matters too. A half swing launches lower and holds its line better than a full one, which makes the 9:00 shot a handy tool on a gusty day.", "Practice plan. Two short sessions a week beat one long one. Spend 15 minutes on the clock, rotating clubs and positions so you never hit the same shot twice in a row. Check your carry numbers again each season.", "The takeaway: one tempo, three backswing lengths, your own written numbers. That is how you stop guessing from 70 yards.", "More: <a href=\"/golf/\">Golf in the 254</a>."], "sources": [["GOLF.com: This clever trick can help you dial in difficult wedge distance control", "https://golf.com/instruction/short-game/clever-trick-wedge-distance-control/"], ["Golf Magic: Gary Boyd clock face wedge distance drill", "https://www.golfmagic.com/instruction/chipping/gary-boyd-clock-face-wedge-distance-drill/16446"]]},
{"id":"baylor-beats-alabama-68-63-players-era-gonzaga-next","seo":"Baylor beats No. 15 Alabama 68-63, faces Gonzaga next","cat":"sports","city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-25","basis":"summary","top":1,"title":"Baylor basketball beats No. 15 Alabama 68-63 in Las Vegas, faces No. 22 Gonzaga next","dek":"Baylor beat No. 15 Alabama 68-63 at the Players Era tournament in Las Vegas, ending a 16-game skid against ranked teams. Gonzaga is next.","body":["Baylor men's basketball beat No. 15 Alabama 68-63 on Tuesday, Nov. 24, at the Players Era tournament in Las Vegas, improving to 5-1 and snapping a 16-game losing streak against ranked opponents, according to Field Level Media and the ESPN box score.","Kayden Mingo led the Bears with 19 points, and he scored four of them in the final 36 seconds to close it out, per the Field Level Media game story.","Next up is No. 22 Gonzaga, which routed Kansas State 101-61 on Tuesday. The Bears and Zags play Thursday, Nov. 26 (Thanksgiving) in Las Vegas. Published tip times conflict, so check ESPN listings before the game.","This story summarizes reporting from Field Level Media and the ESPN game page. Baylor opened the Players Era trip after a 104-55 home win over Jackson State on Nov. 18. Earlier coverage: <a href=\"/news/baylor-week-alabama-las-vegas-wbb-volleyball-houston/\">Baylor's Thanksgiving week schedule</a>.","Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],"sources":[["Field Level Media: Baylor holds off No. 15 Alabama","https://fieldlevelmedia.com/ncaab/baylor-holds-off-no-15-alabama-to-halt-16-game-skid-vs-ranked-teams/"],["ESPN box score: Baylor vs. Alabama","https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/game/_/gameId/401906762/baylor-alabama"],["K-State Sports: Gonzaga 101, Kansas State 61","https://www.kstatesports.com/news/2026/11/25/mens-basketball-k-state-falls-to-no-22-20-gonzaga-at-players-era-16"]]},
{"id":"7-brew-coffee-killeen-fort-hood-street","seo":"7 Brew Coffee plans Fort Hood Street drive-thru in Killeen","cat":"business","city":"Killeen","date":"2026-11-25","basis":"summary","also":["real-estate"],"title":"7 Brew Coffee plans drive-thru on Fort Hood Street in Killeen","dek":"7 Brew Coffee plans a $1.5 million drive-thru at 1080 S. Fort Hood St. in Killeen, with construction set for March to July 2027.","body":["7 Brew Coffee plans a new drive-thru coffee stand at 1080 S. Fort Hood St. in Killeen, a vacant commercial lot in Bell County, according to the Killeen Daily Herald, which cited the state construction filing for the $1.5 million project.","The filing describes a 510-square-foot building, privately funded, with construction scheduled from March 8 to July 9, 2027. The tenant is listed as 7Crew Enterprises LLC and the designer as Arkifex Studios of Springfield, Missouri. No opening date has been announced.","This would be in addition to a Killeen 7 Brew at 3008 W. Stan Schlueter Loop, which the city's second-quarter 2026 development report listed as about half built, per the Herald.","The chain has been expanding across the 254, including two Waco stores on New Road and Hewitt Drive. This story summarizes the Killeen Daily Herald's report; the state filing is listed as TDLR project TABS2027003273.","See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen Daily Herald: 7 Brew Coffee plans Killeen location","https://kdhnews.com/business/7-brew-coffee-plans-killeen-location-as-commercial-development-continues/article_3483c42f-1c15-49e0-8662-ee57493c0e73.html"],["Zabalist: Killeen construction filings","https://www.zabalist.com/projects/city/killeen"]]},
{"id":"central-national-bank-waco-bosque-blvd-5-8-million","seo":"Central National Bank plans $5.8M Bosque Blvd. site in Waco","cat":"business","city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-25","basis":"summary","also":["real-estate"],"title":"Central National Bank plans $5.8 million build-out at 4901 Bosque Blvd. in Waco","dek":"Central National Bank plans a $5.8 million, 16,466-square-foot build-out at 4901 Bosque Blvd. in Waco, aiming for move-in around June 2027.","body":["Central National Bank plans a $5.8 million build-out of 16,466 square feet at 4901 Bosque Blvd. in Waco, across from the Wooded Acres H-E-B, according to Intelligence360, which cited state and local development sources.","The building previously housed Cadence Bank and, before that, Huntington. Occupancy is targeted for about June 1, 2027, per the report. The Waco Buzz newsletter also noted the project on Nov. 24.","Central National Bank is a Waco-based bank founded in 1977 with more than $1 billion in assets, per Intelligence360. The bank has not published details of what will move into the building.","This story summarizes reports from Intelligence360 and The Waco Buzz; we have not yet located the state construction filing.","Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],"sources":[["Intelligence360: Central National Bank plans $5.8M Waco project","https://intelligence360.news/central-national-bank-plans-5800000-00-project-in-waco-texas/"],["The Waco Buzz, Nov. 24, 2026","https://www.thewacobuzz.com/p/a-thanksgiving-question-that-gets-spicy"]]},
{"id":"first-baptist-temple-14-million-childrens-wing","seo":"First Baptist Temple files $14M children's wing on W. Adams","cat":"growth","city":"Temple","date":"2026-11-25","basis":"summary","title":"First Baptist Church of Temple files $14 million children's wing on West Adams Avenue","dek":"First Baptist Church of Temple plans a $14 million, 31,355-square-foot children's wing at 8015 W. Adams Ave., with work set for 2028.","body":["First Baptist Church of Temple plans a $14 million children's wing at its campus at 8015 W. Adams Ave. in Temple, Bell County, according to a state construction filing reported by the Temple Daily Telegram.","The addition would cover about 31,355 square feet. Work is scheduled from Jan. 1 to Aug. 1, 2028, per the report. The filing is listed as TDLR project TABS2027002830, registered Oct. 6, 2026.","The project was one of several east Bell County filings the Telegram tallied at nearly $40 million. Others include a $1.2 million <a href=\"/news/horizon-bank-little-river-academy-branch/\">Horizon Bank branch in Little River-Academy</a> and a $131,603 kids' barbershop, Sharkey's Cuts for Kids, at 7018 Crossroads Way in Temple. The same report's Belton warehouse park was covered earlier: <a href=\"/news/bell-county-filings-belton-warehouse-killeen-fire-station/\">Belton warehouse and Killeen fire station filings</a>.","This story summarizes the Temple Daily Telegram's report, published by the Killeen Daily Herald.","Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],"sources":[["Temple Daily Telegram via KDH: East Bell County to see nearly $40 million in projects","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/east-bell-county-to-see-nearly-40-million-in-commercial-community-projects-as-growth-continues/article_614d2d7a-0fbd-5dd2-a5d8-ca84240cca0a.html"],["Zabalist: Temple construction filings","https://www.zabalist.com/projects/city/temple"]]},
{"id":"horizon-bank-little-river-academy-branch","cat":"business","city":"Little River-Academy","date":"2026-11-25","basis":"summary","title":"Horizon Bank plans new branch in Little River-Academy","dek":"Horizon Bank plans a $1.2 million branch with a drive-thru at 900 E. Main St. in Little River-Academy, with groundbreaking set for Dec. 1.","body":["Horizon Bank plans a $1.2 million branch with a drive-thru at 900 E. Main St. in Little River-Academy, in east Bell County, according to a state construction filing reported by the Temple Daily Telegram.","The building would be about 1,680 square feet. Groundbreaking is set for Dec. 1, with completion expected around June 1, 2027, per the report. The filing is listed as TDLR project TABS2027004061.","The branch was part of nearly $40 million in east Bell County projects tallied by the Telegram, led by a <a href=\"/news/first-baptist-temple-14-million-childrens-wing/\">$14 million children's wing at First Baptist Church of Temple</a>.","This story summarizes the Temple Daily Telegram's report, published by the Killeen Daily Herald.","See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],"sources":[["Temple Daily Telegram via KDH: East Bell County to see nearly $40 million in projects","https://kdhnews.com/news/region/east-bell-county-to-see-nearly-40-million-in-commercial-community-projects-as-growth-continues/article_614d2d7a-0fbd-5dd2-a5d8-ca84240cca0a.html"],["Zabalist: Little River-Academy construction filings","https://www.zabalist.com/projects/city/little-river-academy"]]},
{"id":"waco-ale-co-closes-austin-ave-waco-brewing-co-franklin","seo":"Waco Ale Co. closes Austin Ave. taproom, moving to Franklin","cat":"business","city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-25","basis":"summary","title":"Waco Ale Co. closes Austin Avenue taproom ahead of move to Franklin Avenue as Waco Brewing Co.","dek":"Waco Ale Co. is closing its Austin Avenue taproom as it prepares to reopen as Waco Brewing Co. at 1004 Franklin Ave. in downtown Waco.","body":["Waco Ale Co. is closing its Austin Avenue taproom in downtown Waco as it gets ready to reopen as Waco Brewing Co. at 1004 Franklin Ave. in the coming months, according to The Waco Buzz newsletter. A closing date and reopening date were not given.","KXXV reported in September 2025 that owners Austin and Taylor Brock planned the new space to be nearly five times larger, with a playground, arcade, pickleball court and an expanded food menu. At that time they hoped to open by the end of 2025, so the move is running about a year behind that target.","This story summarizes The Waco Buzz and KXXV. The closing has been reported by one outlet so far; we will update when the brewery announces dates.","See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],"sources":[["The Waco Buzz: Two Austin Ave. staples say goodbye","https://www.thewacobuzz.com/p/two-austin-ave-staples-say-goodbye"],["KXXV: Waco Ale Co. expands to larger downtown location","https://www.kxxv.com/news/local-news/in-your-neighborhood/waco-ale-co-expands-to-larger-downtown-location-rebrands-as-waco-brewing-co-before-year-end"]]},
{"id":"baylor-no-3-learning-communities-us-news","seo":"Baylor ranks No. 3 for learning communities, U.S. News","cat":"education","city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-25","basis":"summary","title":"Baylor ranks No. 3 in the nation for learning communities in U.S. News rankings","dek":"Baylor University ranks No. 3 nationally for learning communities in U.S. News & World Report, its fourth straight year in the top 10.","body":["Baylor University in Waco ranks No. 3 in the nation for learning communities in the U.S. News & World Report undergraduate rankings, the university announced Nov. 20, marking its fourth straight year in the top 10.","Baylor said it is first in Texas, the Big 12, among large private universities and among Christian universities in that category. Learning communities group students who live together and share classes or a theme, often in residence halls.","The university also placed in the top 10 for first-year experience and in the top 40 for both undergraduate teaching and undergraduate research, according to its announcement.","This story summarizes Baylor's announcement. Earlier this week: <a href=\"/news/baylor-time-best-colleges-future-leaders-2027/\">Baylor on TIME's best colleges list</a>."],"sources":[["Baylor University: Baylor jumps to No. 3 nationally for best learning communities","https://www2.baylor.edu/baylorproud/2026/11/baylor-jumps-to-no-3-nationally-for-best-learning-communities"]]},
{"id":"killeen-lets-clear-that-up-rumor-program","seo":"Killeen launches 'Let's Clear That Up' rumor-check program","cat":"government","city":"Killeen","date":"2026-11-25","basis":"summary","title":"Killeen launches 'Let's Clear That Up, Killeen' to answer rumors about city business","dek":"The City of Killeen started a program Nov. 24 where residents can send in rumors about city business and get verified answers from staff.","body":["The City of Killeen launched \"Let's Clear That Up, Killeen\" on Nov. 24, a program run by its Communications and Marketing team to answer rumors and correct misinformation about city business, the Killeen Daily Herald reported.","Residents can send a question to communications@killeentexas.gov with \"Rumor Inquiry\" in the subject line. Staff will research it and reply with verified information, and answers are posted on the city's Clear That Up web page.","The launch comes as the council works through a busy stretch, including filling the District 1 seat left by former Mayor Pro Tem Jessica Gonzalez's resignation (<a href=\"/news/killeen-council-gonzalez-resigns-district-1/\">earlier story</a>) and a <a href=\"/news/killeen-water-wastewater-impact-fees-dec-8-vote/\">Dec. 8 vote on water and wastewater impact fees</a>.","This story summarizes the Killeen Daily Herald's report. Who's who at Killeen City Hall: <a href=\"/local-government/#killeen\">Who Runs the 254</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen Daily Herald: Killeen government creates system to address rumors","https://kdhnews.com/news/local/killeen-govt-creates-system-to-address-rumors-and-transparency-issues/article_63ee8f38-582d-4228-9556-179502de6ce7.html"],["City of Killeen: Let's Clear That Up","https://www.killeentexas.gov/ClearThatUp"]]},
{"id":"mclennan-county-travis-letter-plaque-courthouse","seo":"McLennan County accepts Alamo Travis letter plaque","cat":"government","city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-25","basis":"summary","title":"McLennan County accepts bronze Alamo 'Travis letter' plaque for courthouse plaza","dek":"McLennan County commissioners accepted a donated bronze replica of William Barret Travis's Alamo letter for the Waco courthouse plaza, likely in 2027.","body":["McLennan County commissioners voted unanimously to accept a donated bronze replica of William Barret Travis's 1836 letter from the Alamo, which will be installed at the back of the county courthouse in Waco near the new plaza, KWTX reported Nov. 17.","The plaque weighs about 200 pounds and was paid for by local donors, including the Sons of the Republic of Texas, according to KWTX. Installation is expected in 2027, after upgrades to the justice center area and a pedestrian promenade that will replace an alley. No cost to the county was reported.","This story summarizes KWTX's report. Who sits on the McLennan County Commissioners Court: <a href=\"/local-government/#mclennan-county\">Who Runs the 254</a>."],"sources":[["KWTX: McLennan County accepts Travis letter plaque","https://www.kwtx.com/2026/11/17/mclennan-county-accepts-travis-letter-plaque-courthouse-plaza/"]]},
{"id": "wine-basics-texas-vs-for-sale-in-texas", "cat": "things-to-do", "city": "Central Texas", "date": "2026-11-26", "author": "jake-ruse", "basis": "original", "title": "Wine Basics: 'Texas' vs. 'For Sale in Texas Only' on a Label", "dek": "A Texas appellation tells you where the grapes grew. 'For sale in Texas only' just tells you where the bottle can be sold. Here's how to read both.", "body": ["Short answer: \"Texas\" on the appellation line is a promise about where the grapes grew, while \"For sale in Texas only\" is a promise about where the bottle can be sold, and nothing more.", "Start with the appellation. That's the place-of-origin line on the label, and it's a legal claim. U.S. label law (TTB) says a wine labeled with a state name, like \"Texas,\" must be at least 75 percent from fruit grown in that state and finished there or in a neighboring state. Narrow it to a county and the federal minimum is still 75 percent. Name an American Viticultural Area (AVA), a federally recognized grape-growing region like Texas High Plains or Texas Hill Country, and it jumps to 85 percent.", "Texas goes further than the feds. Texas law says that for grapes harvested from January 1, 2022 on, a wine using a Texas county, a Texas AVA or a Texas vineyard name must be 100 percent Texas fruit. No blending in California juice to stretch a short crop. So when you see \"Texas High Plains\" or \"Texas Hill Country\" on a current bottle, every grape in it grew here.", "Now the other phrase. \"For sale in Texas only\" has nothing to do with grapes. Every wine label normally needs federal approval before it ships. A winery that sells a wine only inside the state where it was bottled can take a federal exemption from that approval instead, and the trade-off is that each bottle has to say \"For sale in\" plus the state. That's the whole meaning. It's a sales boundary, not an origin claim.", "Myth-buster: plenty of people read that line as \"made in Texas from Texas grapes.\" It isn't. A Texas winery can buy grapes or juice from another state, ferment and bottle it here, and sell it under that line. That's legal, and some of it is perfectly good wine. The issue is only when you think you're buying Texas fruit and you're not.", "Here's my pro move in the aisle: skip the front label and find the appellation line, usually near the vintage or the varietal name. Texas, a Texas county or a Texas AVA means Texas grapes, at the percentages above. \"American\" or no place name at all means the fruit could have come from anywhere. At a tasting room, ask it straight: \"Where were the grapes for this one grown?\" A good winery answers that in one breath and is proud to.", "Takeaway: the appellation tells you where the grapes grew; \"For sale in Texas only\" tells you where the bottle is allowed to go.", "More from Jake: <a href=\"/sip-the-254/\">Sip the 254</a>."], "sources": [["TTB: Wine labeling, appellation of origin", "https://ttb.gov/regulated-commodities/beverage-alcohol/wine/labeling-wine/wine-labeling-appellation-of-origin", "record"], ["Texas Legislature: HB 1957 (2021), Alcoholic Beverage Code 101.673", "https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/87R/billtext/html/HB01957F.HTM", "record"], ["TTB Form 5100.31: certificate of label approval or exemption", "https://www.ttb.gov/system/files/images/pdfs/forms/f510031.pdf", "record"]]},
{"id":"rowan-data-center-temple-second-building-780-million","seo":"Rowan Data Center Temple: $780M Second Building Filed","cat":"growth","top":1,"city":"Temple","date":"2026-11-26","basis":"summary","title":"Rowan Digital Infrastructure files plans for a $780 million second data center building in Temple","dek":"A state construction filing shows a 500,000-square-foot, $780 million second building at Rowan's data center site at 1855 Bob White Road in Temple.","body":["Rowan Digital Infrastructure has filed plans for a second data center building in Temple worth an estimated $780 million, according to a state construction filing for the site at 1855 Bob White Road in Bell County.","The filing, registered with the Texas Department of Licensing and Regulation on July 24 as project TABS2026026121, describes a one-story steel building of about 500,000 square feet. The project is named \"AUS02\" (Building 2). Construction is scheduled to run from Aug. 28, 2026, to Aug. 27, 2027. We read the filing through Zabalist, which republishes state construction records, and Data Center Dynamics also reported on it.","That dollar figure is the construction value the owner reported to the state. For scale, the Wilsonart building filed in Temple this month lists $13.5 million.","The filing does not list a tenant, job count or power load, and we have not seen a city or Temple EDC announcement about this building. We will update this story when the city, the EDC or the company releases more details.","Temple's industrial base has been growing fast. Read where East Penn, Sesajal and SeAH stand in <a href=\"/news/temple-industrial-park-2026/\">Temple's industrial park keeps adding up</a>, and see every project we track at <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/rowan-data-center-aus02-temple/\">Coming to the 254</a>.","Planning a commercial project? Visit <a href=\"/build/\">254 Build & Facilities</a>."],"sources":[["Zabalist: TDLR filing TABS2026026121 (Rowan AUS02)","https://www.zabalist.com/projects/TABS2026026121"],["Data Center Dynamics: Rowan files for second building at Temple campus","https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/rowan-files-for-second-building-at-data-center-campus-in-temple-texas/"]]},
{"id":"third-space-contrast-therapy-studio-killeen","seo":"Third Space Contrast Therapy Studio Opening in Killeen","cat":"business","city":"Killeen","date":"2026-11-26","basis":"summary","title":"Third Space contrast therapy studio to open in Killeen with saunas, cold plunges and vitamin C showers","dek":"Third Space, billed as Killeen's first contrast therapy studio, plans to open within weeks at 1200 Lowes Blvd. Here's what it offers and its hours.","body":["Third Space, which its founder says will be the first contrast therapy studio in Killeen, plans to open in the next few weeks at 1200 Lowes Blvd., Suite 108, in the Expressway Plaza Shops in Bell County, the Killeen Daily Herald reported Nov. 24.","The founder, Noel Tavarez, is a former Fort Hood soldier. He told the Herald a year of living in London gave him the idea.","Contrast therapy means switching between heat and cold. At Third Space, customers book a private suite with an infrared sauna that has red-light therapy, a cold plunge and a vitamin C shower. Sessions run about an hour. The studio plans to sell memberships and passes, plus drinks and shower filters.","Planned hours are 7 a.m. to 10 p.m. on weekdays and 10 a.m. to 7 p.m. on weekends. No firm opening date has been announced; the business website is thirdspacetexas.com.","A state construction filing for the space, registered in August under owner Noel Tavarez Rodriguez, lists a $125,000 interior finish-out of about 1,055 square feet.","See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen Daily Herald: Contrast therapy studio to open in Killeen","https://kdhnews.com/business/cold-plunge-saunas-vitamin-c-showers-contrast-therapy-studio-to-open-in-killeen/article_ae0b62c3-db78-4821-ab81-a2375cc5d37f.html"],["Zabalist: TDLR filing TABS2026027331","https://www.zabalist.com/projects/TABS2026027331"]]},
{"id":"klean-kuts-n-kicks-killeen-barbershop-sneaker-restoration","seo":"K'lean Kuts N Kicks: Killeen Barbershop and Sneaker Shop","cat":"business","city":"Killeen","date":"2026-11-26","basis":"summary","title":"K'lean Kuts N Kicks pairs a barbershop with sneaker restoration in Killeen","dek":"A mother and son run K'lean Kuts N Kicks on East Stan Schlueter Loop in Killeen: haircuts for all ages plus sneaker cleaning and repair.","body":["K'lean Kuts N Kicks, a Killeen shop run by Jacqueline \"Jackie\" Hayes and her son, combines a barbershop with a sneaker cleaning and restoration counter at 4200 E. Stan Schlueter Loop in Bell County, according to reports by the Killeen Daily Herald and KTEM.","The barbers cut hair for men, women and children, with a focus on children with special needs, and walk-ins are welcome.","On the sneaker side, the shop cleans shoes, reglues soles, restores the color of suede and removes yellowing. KTEM reported the shop also sells new sneakers.","The idea grew out of her son's sneaker reselling, which he started on Instagram in 2020 before pitching a storefront in 2022, the Herald reported. The two outlets spell his first name differently, so we have left it out until we can confirm it.","See everything opening and closing: <a href=\"/coming-to-the-254/\">Coming to the 254</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen Daily Herald: Mother-son duo brings sneaker restoration and barber services together","https://kdhnews.com/business/mother-son-duo-brings-sneaker-restoration-barber-services-together-in-killeen/article_b964deea-c85e-48a0-9f05-9405e254fd7c.html"],["KTEM: Jackie and Antoine Hayes barber shop","https://ktemnews.com/ixp/513/p/jackie-antoine-hayes-barber-shop/"]]},
{"id":"killeen-council-dec-1-district-1-timeline-fort-hood-street-closure","seo":"Killeen Council Dec. 1: District 1 Vacancy, Road Closure","cat":"government","city":"Killeen","date":"2026-11-26","basis":"records","title":"Killeen council will set the District 1 appointment timeline Dec. 1 and approve a Fort Hood Street closure","dek":"The Killeen City Council's Dec. 1 agenda sets a timeline to fill the District 1 seat, closes part of N. Fort Hood Street Dec. 2-4 and hears two rezonings.","body":["The Killeen City Council will set a timeline Tuesday, Dec. 1, for taking applications and interviewing candidates to fill the District 1 seat left open by Mayor Pro Tem Jessica Gonzalez's resignation, according to the council's posted agenda. The meeting starts at 5 p.m. at City Hall, 101 N. College St., in Bell County.","The item (RS-26-193) formally acknowledges Gonzalez's resignation. The agenda does not list the application dates or name a new mayor pro tem. On Nov. 17 the council voted 7-0 to have staff propose dates, and District 1 residents will get two weeks to apply, the Killeen Daily Herald reported. The appointee will serve until the November 2027 election. Read our earlier story: <a href=\"/news/killeen-council-gonzalez-resigns-district-1/\">Gonzalez resigns</a>.","Also on the consent agenda:","<strong>N. Fort Hood Street closure.</strong> An agreement with TxDOT would temporarily close N. Fort Hood Street (SH 195) between W. Green Avenue and W. Rancier Avenue from Dec. 2 to Dec. 4 for public safety. Several Killeen schools and city offices are already set to close Dec. 3; see <a href=\"/news/killeen-dec-3-closures-schools-city-offices/\">what's closed</a>.","<strong>Fuel contract.</strong> A five-year fuel services agreement with FleetCor Technologies Operating Company through the OMNIA Partners purchasing cooperative, estimated at $2,555,779 in fiscal 2027 and about $13.57 million over five years.","<strong>Boards and change orders.</strong> Council members would be assigned to boards and committees, and vacant board seats filled. A change order cuts $71,252.52 from the Stagecoach Road reconstruction (Phase 1) contract with JHL Construction, and another adds $139,215.39 to the Lift Station No. 6 contract with Bell Contractors Inc.","<strong>Rezonings.</strong> Public hearings are set on rezoning about 1.44 acres at 5505 Bunny Trail from single-family (R-1) to B-2 business, and about 1.12 acres on the west side of Featherline Road to B-4 for GWC Holdings LLC. The council will also get its quarterly financial report and discuss homelessness services.","Who's on the council and how to speak at a meeting: <a href=\"/local-government/#killeen\">Who Runs the 254: Killeen</a>."],"sources":[["Killeen City Council agenda, Dec. 1, 2026","https://killeen.legistar.com/View.ashx?M=A&ID=1456378&GUID=038C3A2F-1933-44F9-9FBD-3FF9849E5B14","record"],["Killeen Daily Herald: Gonzalez turns in resignation","https://kdhnews.com/government/gonzalez-turns-in-resignation-intends-to-stay-on-killeen-council-until-replacement-selected/article_0263ac4c-1ad0-4cf3-af25-ef6c69f315eb.html"]]},
{"id":"mortgage-rates-dip-7-21-254-payment","seo":"Mortgage Rates Dip to 7.21%: What It Means in the 254","cat":"real-estate","city":"Central Texas","date":"2026-11-26","basis":"records","title":"Mortgage rates dip to 7.21% before Thanksgiving. Here's the payment on a typical 254 home","dek":"Freddie Mac's 30-year average fell to 7.21%. On a $275,000 Killeen-Temple home with 10% down, that's about $1,682 a month in principal and interest.","body":["Short answer: at this week's 7.21% average, a buyer putting 10% down on a $275,000 home, the Killeen-Temple median list price, would pay about $1,682 a month in principal and interest, roughly $11 less than a week ago.","Freddie Mac's weekly survey, released a day early on Wednesday, Nov. 25, because of Thanksgiving, put the 30-year fixed average at 7.21%, down from 7.28% the week before. A year ago it was 6.23%. The 15-year average fell to 6.54% from 6.66%.","Daily numbers moved the same way. Mortgage News Daily's 30-year index slipped to 7.26% on Wednesday, down 0.06 point from Tuesday, and its 15-year index fell to 6.82%.","The year-ago comparison is the one that stings. At last year's 6.23%, the same $247,500 loan would cost about $1,521 a month, so today's buyer pays about $161 more each month, or close to $1,900 a year, before taxes and insurance.","Prices are helping a little. Realtor.com data shows the Killeen-Temple median list price down about 7% from a year ago in October, and Waco's down about 4%. Our <a href=\"/real-estate/#housing-dashboard\">254 Housing Dashboard</a> has a payment calculator with local tax rates. See last week's numbers: <a href=\"/news/mortgage-rates-jump-728-254-payment/\">rates jump back to 7.28%</a>.","This is general information, not financial advice."],"sources":[["Freddie Mac: Mortgage Rates Dip to 7.21% (Nov. 25, 2026)","https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/11/25/3410486/0/en/mortgage-rates-dip-to-7-21.html","record"],["Mortgage News Daily: 30-year fixed index","https://www.mortgagenewsdaily.com/mortgage-rates/30-year-fixed"],["FRED: Killeen-Temple median listing price","https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MEDLISPRI28660","record"]]},
{"id":"baylor-volleyball-sweeps-west-virginia-cincinnati-finale","seo":"Baylor Volleyball Sweeps West Virginia 3-0","cat":"sports","city":"Waco","date":"2026-11-26","basis":"summary","title":"No. 20 Baylor volleyball sweeps West Virginia, closes the regular season at Cincinnati Friday","dek":"No. 20 Baylor beat West Virginia 25-22, 25-19, 26-24 in Morgantown to reach 18-9 before Friday's 1 p.m. finale at Cincinnati.","body":["No. 20 Baylor swept West Virginia 3-0 on Wednesday, Nov. 25, at Hope Coliseum in Morgantown, winning 25-22, 25-19, 26-24 to improve to 18-9 overall and 10-7 in the Big 12, according to West Virginia's game recap.","The Bears had to close out a tight third set, winning it by two after the Mountaineers pushed it past 25.","Baylor finishes the regular season Friday, Nov. 27, at Cincinnati at 1 p.m. Central at Fifth Third Arena, streamed on ESPN+. Baylor's preview said the Bears are in the conversation to host first- and second-round NCAA Tournament matches. The bracket is announced after the regular season; we have not confirmed the selection show date.","Scores, schedules and the playoff tracker: <a href=\"/scoreboard/\">254 Scoreboard</a>."],"sources":[["WVU Sports: Mountaineers fall to No. 20 Baylor in three sets","https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/25/volleyball-mountaineers-fall-to-no-20-baylor-in-three-sets"],["Baylor Athletics: Volleyball closes regular season at WVU and Cincinnati","https://baylorbears.com/news/2026/11/24/volleyball-no-20-vb-closes-regular-season-on-the-road-against-wvu-and-cincinnati"]]},
{"id":"weekend-in-the-254-small-business-saturday-nov-27-29","seo":"Things to Do This Weekend in Temple, Belton, Salado, Waco","cat":"things-to-do","city":"Central Texas","date":"2026-11-26","basis":"summary","title":"Weekend in the 254: Small Business Saturday, Salado's Trail of Lights and Reverend Horton Heat in Waco","dek":"Things to do Nov. 27-29 in Temple, Belton, Salado and Waco: holiday markets, light shows, live music, kids' programs and Small Business Saturday.","body":["Black Friday weekend in the 254 runs from Waco's Homestead Fair to the first night of Salado's Tablerock Trail of Lights on Saturday, Nov. 28, with Small Business Saturday markets in Temple and Belton and live music in all four towns. Our <a href=\"/news/thanksgiving-weekend-254-2026/\">Thanksgiving weekend guide</a> has the big ones; here's more, city by city.","<strong>Temple.</strong> Temple High School Theatre hosts a Charlie Brown Christmas Brunch at 10 a.m. Saturday with games and photos with the Peanuts gang. The Catch Vendor Market sets up at Bold Republic Brewing from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m. Saturday for Small Business Saturday. That afternoon, Christmas at the Plaza runs 2 to 8 p.m. at Santa Fe Plaza, with the tree lighting at 7:30 p.m. On Sunday, 3 Texans Winery holds a $50 Christmas manger sip-and-paint.","<strong>Belton.</strong> The Merry Mistletoe Marketplace fills the Expo Center Friday through Sunday ($8 adults, kids 12 and under free). Nature in Lights, the 5.5-mile drive-through display at BLORA, runs nightly from 5:30 to 11 p.m. ($25 a car). Jon Colambo plays Fire Street Pizza at 6 p.m. Saturday.","<strong>Salado.</strong> The Tablerock Trail of Lights opens Saturday, 6 to 10 p.m., with entry by donation. Main Street has Small Business Saturday shopping, Smokin' Maxx at Empresario Wines from 5 to 7 p.m. and live music at The Local Vine from 5 to 8 p.m. Sunday brings Family Fun Day at Bar 1859 (kids can build a pizza for $10) and a free Dalton Gazette set at Empresario from 3 to 5 p.m.","<strong>Waco.</strong> Homestead Fair runs Friday through Sunday with free admission. Wild Lights opens at Cameron Park Zoo, and Christmas at the Silos starts at Magnolia. Mayborn Museum has Fossil Friday at 10:30 a.m., Waco Civic Theatre opens Annie, and the Downtown Farmers Market is 9 a.m. to 1 p.m. Saturday. For a night out: AJ Castillo Friday and The Reverend Horton Heat Saturday at The Backyard, or the Elf Fork & Flick dinner Saturday at AC Hotel.","Times and prices can change, so check each event's page before you go. Filter every event by city, kids, date night and free on our <a href=\"/things-to-do/\">Things to Do guide</a>."],"sources":[["Homestead Fair","https://www.homesteadfair.com/"],["Cameron Park Zoo calendar","https://www.cameronparkzoo.com/calendar-of-events"],["City of Temple: Holly Jolly celebration","https://city-of-temple.prowly.com/467925-city-of-temple-announces-return-of-holly-jolly-month-long-holiday-celebration"],["Merry Mistletoe Marketplace tickets","https://www.tickettailor.com/events/samishow/2075031"],["Fort Hood: Nature in Lights","https://forthoodmediacenter.com/fort-hood-nature-in-lights-returns-nov-20-with-holiday-displays-family-activities/"],["Salado Village Voice: Family Fun Day at Bar 1859","https://saladovillagevoice.com/event/family-fun-day-at-bar-1859/2026-11-29/"],["Visit Salado: Live music at The Local Vine","https://www.visitsaladotexas.com/events/live-music-at-the-local-vine/?gde=2026-11-28"],["Mayborn Museum: Fossil Friday","https://mayborn.web.baylor.edu/event/2026/1556274"],["The Reverend Horton Heat tickets","https://www.etix.com/ticket/p/90313876"]]},
{"id":"hike-steep-climbs-easy-knees","cat":"things-to-do","city":"Central Texas","date":"2026-11-26","trail":"advanced","basis":"original","title":"Hit Harder Trails: Steep Climbs, Easy Knees","dek":"How to climb and descend steep, rocky Central Texas trails like Cameron Park using the rest step, bent knees and trekking poles.","body":["Short answer: on steep climbs, slow down and use the rest step. On the way down, keep your knees bent, shorten your stride and let trekking poles take some of the load. That is how you hike harder terrain without your legs and knees paying for it later.","The rest step is the uphill trick. The Mountaineers teach it for long, steep ascents. With each step forward, straighten and lock your back leg for a beat. That moment shifts your weight onto your skeleton instead of your muscles. Then step again. It feels slow. It is supposed to. A steady pace you can hold beats a fast pace that forces you to stop every few minutes.","Downhill is where knees take the hit. The Mountaineers give a short list. Land with your downhill leg slightly bent so your muscles absorb the impact, not your joints. Keep your weight low and centered over your feet. Do not lean way back or way forward. On steep pitches, take shorter steps. If you carry a pack, cinch the hip belt so it does not swing, and keep it light.","Watch the top of the descent. The Mountaineers note that many slips happen right after a long climb, when legs are tired and attention drifts. Take a breath at the high point and focus on foot placement before you start down.","Trekking poles help on both ends. The American Hiking Society says poles let your arms share the work, which means less knee pain, especially on descents, plus two extra points of contact for balance. REI says poles on downhill sections reduce the work the muscles around your knees and ankles have to do. The American Hiking Society also asks hikers to use rubber tips and keep poles close to the tread so steel tips do not scar rock or widen the trail.","Where to practice in the 254: Cameron Park in Waco is the go-to right now. The city's trail system has about 26 miles of rocky singletrack with short, steep climbs and drops above the Brazos. That makes it a good place to drill the rest step on a climb and the bent-knee, short-step descent on the way back down. Hikers share the trails with mountain bikers, and there are lots of intersections, so carry the city's trail map.","Dana Peak Park in Harker Heights is the other classic hill workout, but the Army Corps closes it October through March. Save it for April.","Limestone adds its own twist. Loose rock rolls and wet rock is slick, so short steps and planted poles matter even more after rain.","Takeaway: slow and steady up, short and bent-kneed down, poles for backup.","More: <a href=\"/trails/\">Trails & Hiking in the 254</a>."],"sources":[["The Mountaineers: Hiking techniques","https://mountaineers.org/locations-lodges/olympia-branch/committees/olympia-hiking-backpacking-committee/course-templates/conditioning-hiking-series-olympia/course-materials/hiking-techniques"],["American Hiking Society: Trekking poles","https://americanhiking.org/trekking-poles/"],["REI Expert Advice: How to recover from a hike","https://www.rei.com/learn/expert-advice/how-to-recover-from-hike.html"],["City of Waco: Cameron Park trail system rules","https://www.waco-texas.com/Departments/Parks-Recreation/Cameron-Park/Cameron-Park-Trail-System-Rules","record"]]},
{"id":"wine-basics-how-to-taste-a-flight","cat":"things-to-do","city":"Central Texas","date":"2026-11-27","author":"jake-ruse","basis":"original","title":"Wine Basics: How to Taste a Flight Like a Pro","dek":"Taste light to heavy and dry to sweet, give each pour four quick steps, and use the dump bucket. Then put it to work in Salado this weekend.","body":["Short answer: go light to heavy and dry to sweet, give every pour the same four quick steps, and dump anything you don't love without apology.","Order matters because your mouth keeps score. Sugar left on your tongue makes the next dry wine taste sharper and thinner than it is. Tannin, the grippy stuff from grape skins and seeds that dries out your gums, coats your mouth so a delicate white poured after a big red tastes like water. So the pro order runs sparkling and crisp whites first, then fuller whites and rosé, lighter reds, bigger reds, and anything sweet or fortified last. Most tasting menus are already printed in that order. Don't freelance it.","The four steps are look, smell, sip, decide. Look: tilt the glass against something white. Whites deepen toward gold as they age; reds fade from purple toward brick. Smell: a short swirl, then a few quick sniffs. Most of what you call flavor comes in through your nose, so don't skip this. Sip: take enough to coat your mouth and hold it a few seconds. Check three things: sweet or dry, acidity (the part that makes your mouth water), and in reds, tannin. Decide: would I drink a whole glass of this? That's the only score that counts.","Myth-buster: the dump bucket is not an insult. Professionals spit and pour out all day because judgment fades fast after a few full pours. Nobody behind the bar is offended when you tip out the last half-ounce of something that isn't for you. That's what the bucket is there for.","Pro move: cleanse with water and a plain cracker between pours, and be careful judging a wine on cheese. Fat and salt soften tannin and round off acidity, so almost every red tastes better with a bite of cheddar. There's an old trade saying for it: buy on apples, sell on cheese. Taste it clean first, then enjoy the pairing.","You don't need tasting notes to talk to the person pouring. Say what you like in plain words, \"dry and crisp\" or \"big red, easy on the oak,\" and ask, \"Which one would you take home?\" You'll get a better answer than any score.","My weekend pick: put this to work at Empresario Wines, 7 N. Main St. in Salado, a 100% Texas wine tasting room that pours bottles from across the state. It's a walk from the Small Business Saturday shopping on Main Street, Smokin' Maxx plays there Saturday from 5 to 7 p.m., and Dalton Gazette plays a free set Sunday from 3 to 5 p.m. Hours change, so check before you go.","Takeaway: light to heavy, dry to sweet, and the only score that matters is whether you'd buy the bottle.","More from Jake: <a href=\"/sip-the-254/\">Sip the 254</a>."],"sources":[["WSET: Systematic Approach to Tasting (Level 2 Wines)","https://www.wsetglobal.com/media/13156/wset_l2wines_sat_en_may2023_issue2.pdf"],["Visit Salado: Empresario Wines","https://visitsaladotexas.com/?p=28504"]]},
];
